10.62.0	data_table/Common Sourdough Stages and Their Timing	<div class="stack"><p class="muted">Times are a guide, feel is the boss, <regex>user_name</regex>.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Stage</th><th class="num">Typical time</th><th>What you're looking for</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Feed starter</td><td class="num">8–12 h</td><td>Doubled, domed, smells of yogurt</td></tr><tr><td>Autolyse</td><td class="num">30–60 min</td><td>Flour and water, no salt yet</td></tr><tr><td>Bulk ferment</td><td class="num">4–6 h</td><td>50–75% rise, jiggly, bubbles at edge</td></tr><tr><td>Shape</td><td class="num">10–15 min</td><td>Taut skin, holds a seam</td></tr><tr><td>Cold retard</td><td class="num">12–36 h</td><td>Fridge nap — flavour builds</td></tr><tr><td>Bake covered</td><td class="num">20 min</td><td>Steam for the spring</td></tr><tr><td>Bake uncovered</td><td class="num">20–25 min</td><td>Deep amber crust, hollow tap</td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class="acc"><summary>Cold kitchen? Stretch it out</summary><div class="body"><p class="t-small">Under 20°C, add roughly 50% to bulk time. Over 27°C, knock 30% off and check sooner.</p></div></details></div>	<div class="stack"><p class="muted">Times are a guide, feel is the boss, .</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Stage</th><th class="num">Typical time</th><th>What you're looking for</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Feed starter</td><td class="num">8–12 h</td><td>Doubled, domed, smells of yogurt</td></tr><tr><td>Autolyse</td><td class="num">30–60 min</td><td>Flour and water, no salt yet</td></tr><tr><td>Bulk ferment</td><td class="num">4–6 h</td><td>50–75% rise, jiggly, bubbles at edge</td></tr><tr><td>Shape</td><td class="num">10–15 min</td><td>Taut skin, holds a seam</td></tr><tr><td>Cold retard</td><td class="num">12–36 h</td><td>Fridge nap — flavour builds</td></tr><tr><td>Bake covered</td><td class="num">20 min</td><td>Steam for the spring</td></tr>