10.8.1	data_table/Common Laundry Symbols and What They Mean	<div class="stack"><h3 class="card-title">Laundry Tag Symbols, Decoded</h3><p class="muted t-small">Because guessing is how sweaters become crop tops, <regex>user_name</regex>.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Symbol</th><th>Means</th><th>Do This</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Bucket + 30</td><td>Wash at 30°C</td><td>Cold cycle, gentle</td></tr><tr><td>Bucket, no number</td><td>Any machine wash</td><td>Cold to warm</td></tr><tr><td>Hand in bucket</td><td>Hand wash only</td><td>Sink, mild soap</td></tr><tr><td>Triangle</td><td>Bleach allowed</td><td>Use if needed</td></tr><tr><td>Square + circle</td><td>Tumble dry okay</td><td>Low heat preferred</td></tr><tr><td>Iron with one dot</td><td>Low heat iron</td><td>Cool setting</td></tr><tr><td>Circle in square, crossed</td><td>No tumble dry</td><td>Hang or lay flat</td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class="acc"><summary>What about the crossed-out ones?</summary><div class="body"><p>A slash through any symbol just means "don't." Crossed bucket = no wash, crossed iron = don't iron, and so on.</p></div></details></div>	<div class="stack"><h3 class="card-title">Laundry Tag Symbols, Decoded</h3><p class="muted t-small">Because guessing is how sweaters become crop tops, .</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Symbol</th><th>Means</th><th>Do This</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Bucket + 30</td><td>Wash at 30°C</td><td>Cold cycle, gentle</td></tr><tr><td>Bucket, no number</td><td>Any machine wash</td><td>Cold to warm</td></tr><tr><td>Hand in bucket</td><td>Hand wash only</td><td>Sink, mild soap</td></tr><tr><td>Triangle</td><td>Bleach allowed</td><td>Use if needed</td></tr><tr><td>Square + circle</td><td>Tumble dry okay</td><td>Low heat preferred</td></tr><tr><td>Iron with one dot</td><td>Low heat iron</td><td>Cool setting</td></tr><tr><td>Circle in square, crossed</td><td>No tumble dry</td><td>Hang