10.10.1	data_table/Common Recycling Codes and What They Accept	<div class="stack"><h3 class="card-title">Recycling Numbers, 1–7</h3><p class="muted t-small">Curbside rules vary by town, <regex>user_name</regex>, so treat this as the general map.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Code</th><th>Plastic</th><th>Common Item</th><th>Usually Accepted?</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="num">1</td><td>PET</td><td>Water &amp; soda bottles</td><td>Yes, widely</td></tr><tr><td class="num">2</td><td>HDPE</td><td>Milk jugs, shampoo</td><td>Yes, widely</td></tr><tr><td class="num">3</td><td>PVC</td><td>Pipes, some wrap</td><td>Rarely</td></tr><tr><td class="num">4</td><td>LDPE</td><td>Bags, squeeze bottles</td><td>Store drop-off</td></tr><tr><td class="num">5</td><td>PP</td><td>Tubs, yogurt cups</td><td>Often yes</td></tr><tr><td class="num">6</td><td>PS</td><td>Foam, clamshells</td><td>Rarely</td></tr><tr><td class="num">7</td><td>Other</td><td>Mixed / polycarbonate</td><td>Almost never</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="callout info"><p>Rinse and dry anything headed for the bin. Food residue is a common reason whole loads get rejected.</p></div></div>	<div class="stack"><h3 class="card-title">Recycling Numbers, 1–7</h3><p class="muted t-small">Curbside rules vary by town, , so treat this as the general map.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Code</th><th>Plastic</th><th>Common Item</th><th>Usually Accepted?</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="num">1</td><td>PET</td><td>Water &amp; soda bottles</td><td>Yes, widely</td></tr><tr><td class="num">2</td><td>HDPE</td><td>Milk jugs, shampoo</td><td>Yes, widely</td></tr><tr><td class="num">3</td><td>PVC</td><td>Pipes, some wrap</td><td>Rarely</td></tr><tr><td class="num">4</td><td>LDPE</td><td>Bags, squeeze bottles</td><td>Store drop-off</td></tr><tr><td class="num">5</td><td>PP</td><td>Tubs, yogurt cups</td><td>Often yes</td></tr><tr><td class="num">6</td><