14.39.0	comparison/Microwave vs. Oven: Which to Reheat?	<div class="grid two"><div class="card"><h4>Microwave</h4><p><strong>Pros:</strong> Fast, energy-efficient, easy cleanup. <strong>Cons:</strong> Soggy textures, uneven heating, rubbery meat.</p><p class="t-small dim">Best for: soups, stews, rice, quick meals.</p></div><div class="card"><h4>Oven</h4><p><strong>Pros:</strong> Restores crispness, even heat, better browning. <strong>Cons:</strong> Slow, heats the kitchen, uses more energy.</p><p class="t-small dim">Best for: pizza, roasted veggies, fried foods.</p></div></div><p class="muted">Reheat wet foods in the microwave. For anything that should be crispy, the oven (or toaster oven) is worth the wait.</p>	<div class="grid two"><div class="card"><h4>Microwave</h4><p><strong>Pros:</strong> Fast, energy-efficient, easy cleanup. <strong>Cons:</strong> Soggy textures, uneven heating, rubbery meat.</p><p class="t-small dim">Best for: soups, stews, rice, quick meals.</p></div><div class="card"><h4>Oven</h4><p><strong>Pros:</strong> Restores crispness, even heat, better browning. <strong>Cons:</strong> Slow, heats the kitchen, uses more energy.</p><p class="t-small dim">Best for: pizza, roasted veggies, fried foods.</p></div></div><p class="muted">Reheat wet foods in the microwave. For anything that should be crispy, the oven (or toaster oven) is worth the wait.</p>	-
