20.7.0	diagram_simple/Bike Chain Repair	<div class="umi-page"><h2 class="card-title">Bike Chain Repair</h2><p class="muted">Hey <regex>user_name</regex>, here's the quick fix for a slipped chain.</p><div class="chart"><svg viewBox="0 0 400 100"><rect x="10" y="30" width="60" height="40" fill="var(--accent-soft)" stroke="var(--line)"></rect><text x="40" y="55" class="lbl">Stop</text><line x1="70" y1="50" x2="120" y2="50" class="axis"></line><rect x="120" y="30" width="60" height="40" fill="var(--info-soft)" stroke="var(--line)"></rect><text x="150" y="55" class="lbl">Shift</text><line x1="180" y1="50" x2="230" y2="50" class="axis"></line><rect x="230" y="30" width="60" height="40" fill="var(--warn-soft)" stroke="var(--line)"></rect><text x="260" y="55" class="lbl">Lift</text><line x1="290" y1="50" x2="340" y2="50" class="axis"></line><rect x="340" y="30" width="60" height="40" fill="var(--good-soft)" stroke="var(--line)"></rect><text x="370" y="55" class="lbl">Seat</text></svg></div><ol class="list"><li>Stop pedaling and shift to the smallest chainring and smallest rear cog.</li><li>Lift the chain onto the teeth of the chainring.</li><li>Slowly pedal forward while shifting up to a middle gear.</li><li>Check chain tension and lubricate if needed.</li></ol><details class="acc"><summary>Pro tips</summary><div class="body"><p>If it keeps happening, your chain might be stretched. A chain checker can tell you in seconds.</p></div></details><p class="t-small dim">Ride safe out there.</p></div>	<div class="umi-page"><h2 class="card-title">Bike Chain Repair</h2><p class="muted">Hey , here's the quick fix for a slipped chain.</p><div class="chart"><svg viewBox="0 0 400 100"><rect x="10" y="30" width="60" height="40" fill="var(--accent-soft)" stroke="var(--line)"></rect><text x="40" y="55" class="lbl">Stop</text><line x1="70" y1="50" x2="120" y2="50" class="axis"></line><rect x="120" y="30" width="60" height="40" fill="var(--info-soft)" stroke="var(--line)"></rect><text x="150"