20.24.1	diagram_simple/Water Cycle in Five Stops	<div class="card"><p class="muted t-small">Here's the short version, <regex>user_name</regex> — five stops, no detours.</p><div class="chart"><svg viewBox="0 0 320 180" role="img" aria-label="Water cycle: evaporation, condensation, precipitation, collection, back to evaporation"><rect x="10" y="70" width="70" height="34" rx="6" fill="var(--accent-soft)" stroke="var(--line)"></rect><text x="45" y="91" class="lbl" text-anchor="middle">Evaporation</text><line x1="80" y1="87" x2="120" y2="87" class="axis"></line><rect x="120" y="70" width="72" height="34" rx="6" fill="var(--accent-soft)" stroke="var(--line)"></rect><text x="156" y="91" class="lbl" text-anchor="middle">Condensation</text><line x1="192" y1="87" x2="232" y2="87" class="axis"></line><rect x="232" y="70" width="78" height="34" rx="6" fill="var(--good-soft)" stroke="var(--line)"></rect><text x="271" y="91" class="lbl" text-anchor="middle">Precipitation</text><line x1="271" y1="104" x2="271" y2="134" class="axis"></line><rect x="120" y="134" width="110" height="34" rx="6" fill="var(--good-soft)" stroke="var(--line)"></rect><text x="175" y="155" class="lbl" text-anchor="middle">Collection</text><line x1="120" y1="151" x2="45" y2="151" class="axis"></line><line x1="45" y1="151" x2="45" y2="104" class="axis"></line></svg></div><details class="acc"><summary>What each stop means</summary><div class="body"><ol class="list"><li>Sun warms water; it rises as vapour.</li><li>Cold air turns vapour into droplets — clouds.</li><li>Droplets get heavy and fall as rain or snow.</li><li>Water lands in rivers, lakes, soil, and the sea.</li></ol></div></details></div>	<div class="card"><p class="muted t-small">Here's the short version,  — five stops, no detours.</p><div class="chart"><svg viewBox="0 0 320 180" role="img" aria-label="Water cycle: evaporation, condensation, precipitation, collection, back to evaporation"><rect x="10" y="70" width="70" 