20.25.1	diagram_simple/Toothpaste Tube Squeeze Path	<div class="card"><p class="muted t-small">Ask away, <regex>user_name</regex>. Squeeze travels, paste follows.</p><div class="chart"><svg viewBox="0 0 320 150" role="img" aria-label="Flow from hand squeeze to ribbon of toothpaste on brush"><rect x="10" y="55" width="80" height="36" rx="6" fill="var(--accent-soft)" stroke="var(--line)"></rect><text x="50" y="77" class="lbl" text-anchor="middle">Hand squeeze</text><line x1="90" y1="73" x2="130" y2="73" class="axis"></line><rect x="130" y="55" width="80" height="36" rx="6" fill="var(--warn-soft)" stroke="var(--line)"></rect><text x="170" y="77" class="lbl" text-anchor="middle">Pressure builds</text><line x1="210" y1="73" x2="250" y2="73" class="axis"></line><rect x="250" y="55" width="60" height="36" rx="6" fill="var(--good-soft)" stroke="var(--line)"></rect><text x="280" y="77" class="lbl" text-anchor="middle">Ribbon</text><path d="M250 120 q15 -10 30 0 q15 10 30 0" fill="none" stroke="var(--ink-3)" stroke-width="3"></path></svg></div><details class="acc"><summary>Why it curls and flattens</summary><div class="body"><p>Paste is thick and holds its shape. The nozzle's flat slit forces it into a ribbon, then gravity does the curling.</p></div></details></div>	<div class="card"><p class="muted t-small">Ask away, . Squeeze travels, paste follows.</p><div class="chart"><svg viewBox="0 0 320 150" role="img" aria-label="Flow from hand squeeze to ribbon of toothpaste on brush"><rect x="10" y="55" width="80" height="36" rx="6" fill="var(--accent-soft)" stroke="var(--line)"></rect><text x="50" y="77" class="lbl" text-anchor="middle">Hand squeeze</text><line x1="90" y1="73" x2="130" y2="73" class="axis"></line><rect x="130" y="55" width="80" height="36" rx="6" fill="var(--warn-soft)" stroke="var(--line)"></rect><text x="170" y="77" class="lbl" text-anchor="middle">Pressure builds</text><line x1="210" y1="73" x2="250" y2="73" class="axis"></line><rect