20.26.1	diagram_simple/Microwave Heating Loop	<div class="card"><p class="muted t-small">One loop, <regex>user_name</regex>. Electricity in, warm leftovers out.</p><div class="chart"><svg viewBox="0 0 320 160" role="img" aria-label="Microwave energy flow from wall power to heated food"><rect x="10" y="60" width="70" height="36" rx="6" fill="var(--panel-2)" stroke="var(--line)"></rect><text x="45" y="82" class="lbl" text-anchor="middle">Wall power</text><line x1="80" y1="78" x2="116" y2="78" class="axis"></line><rect x="116" y="60" width="78" height="36" rx="6" fill="var(--accent-soft)" stroke="var(--line)"></rect><text x="155" y="82" class="lbl" text-anchor="middle">Magnetron</text><line x1="194" y1="78" x2="230" y2="78" class="axis"></line><rect x="230" y="60" width="80" height="36" rx="6" fill="var(--accent-soft)" stroke="var(--line)"></rect><text x="270" y="82" class="lbl" text-anchor="middle">Microwaves</text><line x1="270" y1="96" x2="270" y2="124" class="axis"></line><rect x="190" y="124" width="100" height="30" rx="6" fill="var(--good-soft)" stroke="var(--line)"></rect><text x="240" y="143" class="lbl" text-anchor="middle">Water molecules spin</text></svg></div><details class="acc"><summary>Where the heat comes from</summary><div class="body"><p>Microwaves flip water molecules billions of times a second. Friction between them becomes heat — the dish warms from the food's own water.</p></div></details></div>	<div class="card"><p class="muted t-small">One loop, . Electricity in, warm leftovers out.</p><div class="chart"><svg viewBox="0 0 320 160" role="img" aria-label="Microwave energy flow from wall power to heated food"><rect x="10" y="60" width="70" height="36" rx="6" fill="var(--panel-2)" stroke="var(--line)"></rect><text x="45" y="82" class="lbl" text-anchor="middle">Wall power</text><line x1="80" y1="78" x2="116" y2="78" class="axis"></line><rect x="116" y="60" width="78" height="36" rx="6" fill="var(--accent-soft)" stroke="var(