21.53.0	illustration/Reviving a Dried-Out Pen	<div class="card"><ol class="list"><li>Scribble on scrap paper in tight circles for ten seconds. Half of them just needed a nudge.</li><li>Warm the tip in your fingers for a minute.</li><li>A drop of water on the ball, then scribble again.</li><li>Rubber band the pen tip-down overnight; gravity does the rest.</li></ol><div class="chart"><svg viewBox="0 0 240 110" role="img" aria-label="A pen barrel with ink falling toward the tip"><rect x="80" y="10" width="16" height="62" rx="6" fill="var(--panel-2)" stroke="var(--line)"></rect><path d="M88 72l8 20 8-20z" fill="var(--ink-3)"></path><circle cx="88" cy="46" r="4" fill="var(--accent)"></circle><path d="M104 84h40" stroke="var(--line-2)" stroke-width="2"></path><text x="150" y="88" class="lbl">ink travels down</text><text x="88" y="106" text-anchor="middle" class="lbl">tip</text></svg></div><p class="t-small muted">If it still skips after all that, <regex>user_name</regex>, the ink is truly gone. Retirement time.</p></div>	<div class="card"><ol class="list"><li>Scribble on scrap paper in tight circles for ten seconds. Half of them just needed a nudge.</li><li>Warm the tip in your fingers for a minute.</li><li>A drop of water on the ball, then scribble again.</li><li>Rubber band the pen tip-down overnight; gravity does the rest.</li></ol><div class="chart"><svg viewBox="0 0 240 110" role="img" aria-label="A pen barrel with ink falling toward the tip"><rect x="80" y="10" width="16" height="62" rx="6" fill="var(--panel-2)" stroke="var(--line)"></rect><path d="M88 72l8 20 8-20z" fill="var(--ink-3)"></path><circle cx="88" cy="46" r="4" fill="var(--accent)"></circle><path d="M104 84h40" stroke="var(--line-2)" stroke-width="2"></path><text x="150" y="88" class="lbl">ink travels down</text><text x="88" y="106" text-anchor="middle" class="lbl">tip</text></svg></div><p class="t-small muted">If it still skips after all that, , the ink is truly gone. 