23.3.0	quiz_question/Basic car maintenance quiz	<div class="quiz"><div class="q"><regex>user_name</regex>, how often should you check your tire pressure?</div><details><summary>A) Once a year</summary></details><details><summary>B) Monthly and before long trips</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Tires lose pressure over time, and it's an easy safety win.</div></details><details><summary>C) Only when a tire looks flat</summary></details><details><summary>D) Never, it's overrated</summary></details></div>	<div class="quiz"><div class="q">, how often should you check your tire pressure?</div><details><summary>A) Once a year</summary></details><details><summary>B) Monthly and before long trips</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Tires lose pressure over time, and it's an easy safety win.</div></details><details><summary>C) Only when a tire looks flat</summary></details><details><summary>D) Never, it's overrated</summary></details></div>	-
23.4.0	quiz_question/Chess rules quiz	<div class="quiz"><div class="q"><regex>user_name</regex>, which piece can jump over other pieces?</div><details><summary>A) The rook</summary></details><details><summary>B) The knight</summary><div class="answer">Correct. The knight is the only piece that can leap over others.</div></details><details><summary>C) The bishop</summary></details><details><summary>D) The queen</summary></details></div>	<div class="quiz"><div class="q">, which piece can jump over other pieces?</div><details><summary>A) The rook</summary></details><details><summary>B) The knight</summary><div class="answer">Correct. The knight is the only piece that can leap over others.</div></details><details><summary>C) The bishop</summary></details><details><summary>D) The queen</summary></details></div>	-
23.5.0	quiz_question/Coffee brewing quiz	<div class="quiz"><div class="q"><regex>user_name</regex>, what's the ideal water temperature for brewing coffee?</div><details><summary>A) Boiling (212°F)</summary></details><details><summary>B) Just off the boil, around 200°F</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Boiling water can scorch the grounds and make it bitter.</div></details><details><summary>C) Room temperature</summary></details><details><summary>D) Cold</summary></details></div>	<div class="quiz"><div class="q">, what's the ideal water temperature for brewing coffee?</div><details><summary>A) Boiling (212°F)</summary></details><details><summary>B) Just off the boil, around 200°F</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Boiling water can scorch the grounds and make it bitter.</div></details><details><summary>C) Room temperature</summary></details><details><summary>D) Cold</summary></details></div>	-
23.6.0	quiz_question/Bike safety quiz	<div class="card"><div class="card-title">Bike safety quiz</div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">You're riding at dusk. What's the smartest move?</div><details><summary>A) Trust your reflexes</summary></details><details><summary>B) Wear reflective gear and use lights</summary><div class="answer">Correct. See and be seen. Lights and reflectors cut crash risk at dusk more than any other single step.</div></details><details><summary>C) Ride on the sidewalk</summary></details></div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">Approaching a stop sign with no other cars, you should…</div><details><summary>A) Slow, look, and roll through</summary></details><details><summary>B) Come to a full stop</summary><div class="answer">Correct. It's the law almost everywhere, and it gives you time to spot a hidden car or pedestrian.</div></details><details><summary>C) Wave and go</summary></details></div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">How should you signal a right turn?</div><details><summary>A) Point right arm straight out</summary></details><details><summary>B) Bend left arm up at 90°</summary><div class="answer">Correct. The bent-left-arm signal is the standard for right turns.</div></details><details><summary>C) Just look over your shoulder</summary></details></div><p class="t-small muted">Hey <regex>user_name</regex>, these are the big three. Ride like you're invisible, but act like you're seen.</p></div>	<div class="card"><div class="card-title">Bike safety quiz</div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">You're riding at dusk. What's the smartest move?</div><details><summary>A) Trust your reflexes</summary></details><details><summary>B) Wear reflective gear and use lights</summary><div class="answer">Correct. See and be seen. Lights and reflectors cut crash risk at dusk more than any other single step.</div></details><details><summary>C) Ride on the sidewalk</summary></details></div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">Approaching a stop sign with no other cars, you should…</div><details><summary>A) Slow, look, and roll through</summary></details><details><summary>B) Come to a full stop</summary><div class="answer">Correct. It's the law almost everywhere, and it gives you time to spot a hidden car or pedestrian.</div></details><details><summary>C) Wave and go</summary></details></div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">How should you signal a right turn?</div><details><summary>A) Point right arm straight out</summary></details><details><summary>B) Bend left arm up at 90°</summary><div class="answer">Correct. The bent-left-arm signal is the standard for right turns.</div></details><details><summary>C) Just look over your shoulder</summary></details></div><p class="t-small muted">Hey , these are the big three. Ride like you're invisible, but act like you're seen.</p></div>	-
23.7.0	quiz_question/First aid basics quiz	<div class="card"><div class="card-title">First aid basics quiz</div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">Someone is choking and can't speak. What do you do first?</div><details><summary>A) Give water</summary></details><details><summary>B) Five back blows</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Five back blows between the shoulder blades, then five abdominal thrusts if needed. Call emergency services if it doesn't clear.</div></details><details><summary>C) Lay them down</summary></details></div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">For a minor burn, the best immediate treatment is…</div><details><summary>A) Butter</summary></details><details><summary>B) Ice</summary></details><details><summary>C) Cool running water for 20 minutes</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Cool water reduces damage and pain. Skip ice, butter, and toothpaste.</div></details></div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">How do you check if someone is responsive?</div><details><summary>A) Shake them hard</summary></details><details><summary>B) Tap and shout</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Tap their shoulders and ask loudly, "Are you okay?" If no response, call for help and check breathing.</div></details><details><summary>C) Splash water on their face</summary></details></div><p class="t-small muted"><regex>user_name</regex>, these basics buy time until professionals arrive. Worth knowing cold.</p></div>	<div class="card"><div class="card-title">First aid basics quiz</div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">Someone is choking and can't speak. What do you do first?</div><details><summary>A) Give water</summary></details><details><summary>B) Five back blows</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Five back blows between the shoulder blades, then five abdominal thrusts if needed. Call emergency services if it doesn't clear.</div></details><details><summary>C) Lay them down</summary></details></div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">For a minor burn, the best immediate treatment is…</div><details><summary>A) Butter</summary></details><details><summary>B) Ice</summary></details><details><summary>C) Cool running water for 20 minutes</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Cool water reduces damage and pain. Skip ice, butter, and toothpaste.</div></details></div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">How do you check if someone is responsive?</div><details><summary>A) Shake them hard</summary></details><details><summary>B) Tap and shout</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Tap their shoulders and ask loudly, "Are you okay?" If no response, call for help and check breathing.</div></details><details><summary>C) Splash water on their face</summary></details></div><p class="t-small muted">, these basics buy time until professionals arrive. Worth knowing cold.</p></div>	-
23.8.0	quiz_question/Home fire safety quiz	<div class="card"><div class="card-title">Home fire safety quiz</div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">How often should you test smoke alarms?</div><details><summary>A) Once a year</summary></details><details><summary>B) Once a month</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Monthly tests catch dead batteries before they matter. Replace the units every 10 years.</div></details><details><summary>C) Only when they chirp</summary></details></div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">A pan of oil catches fire. You should…</div><details><summary>A) Throw water on it</summary></details><details><summary>B) Slide a lid over it and turn off the heat</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Smother it. Water makes oil fires explode.</div></details><details><summary>C) Carry it outside</summary></details></div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">Where's the safest place for a space heater?</div><details><summary>A) Next to curtains</summary></details><details><summary>B) On a flat, clear surface 3 feet from anything flammable</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Give it space. Never leave it running unattended or while you sleep.</div></details><details><summary>C) Under a desk</summary></details></div><p class="t-small muted">Nice one, <regex>user_name</regex>. A few minutes now saves a lot of panic later.</p></div>	<div class="card"><div class="card-title">Home fire safety quiz</div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">How often should you test smoke alarms?</div><details><summary>A) Once a year</summary></details><details><summary>B) Once a month</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Monthly tests catch dead batteries before they matter. Replace the units every 10 years.</div></details><details><summary>C) Only when they chirp</summary></details></div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">A pan of oil catches fire. You should…</div><details><summary>A) Throw water on it</summary></details><details><summary>B) Slide a lid over it and turn off the heat</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Smother it. Water makes oil fires explode.</div></details><details><summary>C) Carry it outside</summary></details></div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">Where's the safest place for a space heater?</div><details><summary>A) Next to curtains</summary></details><details><summary>B) On a flat, clear surface 3 feet from anything flammable</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Give it space. Never leave it running unattended or while you sleep.</div></details><details><summary>C) Under a desk</summary></details></div><p class="t-small muted">Nice one, . A few minutes now saves a lot of panic later.</p></div>	-
23.9.0	quiz_question/Personal finance basics quiz	<div class="card"><div class="card-title">Personal finance basics quiz</div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">What's the 50/30/20 rule?</div><details><summary>A) A tax formula</summary></details><details><summary>B) 50% needs, 30% wants, 20% savings</summary><div class="answer">Correct. A simple budget split. Adjust the numbers to fit your life, but keep savings in the mix.</div></details><details><summary>C) A credit score range</summary></details></div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">An emergency fund should cover…</div><details><summary>A) One month of expenses</summary></details><details><summary>B) Three to six months</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Three to six months of essential expenses is the usual target. Start with one month if that feels far off.</div></details><details><summary>C) A year of income</summary></details></div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">Which debt usually costs the most to carry?</div><details><summary>A) Mortgage</summary></details><details><summary>B) Student loans</summary></details><details><summary>C) Credit card</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Credit cards typically have the highest interest. Pay those down first.</div></details></div><p class="t-small muted"><regex>user_name</regex>, small habits beat big intentions. Automate a transfer and forget it.</p></div>	<div class="card"><div class="card-title">Personal finance basics quiz</div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">What's the 50/30/20 rule?</div><details><summary>A) A tax formula</summary></details><details><summary>B) 50% needs, 30% wants, 20% savings</summary><div class="answer">Correct. A simple budget split. Adjust the numbers to fit your life, but keep savings in the mix.</div></details><details><summary>C) A credit score range</summary></details></div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">An emergency fund should cover…</div><details><summary>A) One month of expenses</summary></details><details><summary>B) Three 