23.12.0	quiz_question/Bread baking quiz	<div class="card"><div class="card-title">Bread baking quiz</div><p class="muted">A few questions to see if you're proofing like a pro.</p><div class="quiz"><div class="q">1. What does a sourdough starter need to stay active?</div><details><summary>A) Regular feeding with flour and water</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Feed it regularly and keep it warm.</div></details><details><summary>B) Direct sunlight</summary></details><details><summary>C) A sealed jar in the fridge forever</summary></details></div><div class="divider"></div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">2. What is autolyse?</div><details><summary>A) Letting dough rise twice</summary></details><details><summary>B) Resting flour and water before adding salt and yeast</summary><div class="answer">Correct. It hydrates the flour and builds gluten.</div></details><details><summary>C) Baking at high heat</summary></details></div><div class="divider"></div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">3. How do you know bread is fully baked?</div><details><summary>A) It sounds hollow when tapped</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Internal temp around 200210 ␀F if you have a thermometer.</div></details><details><summary>B) The crust is golden</summary></details><details><summary>C) It has risen</summary></details></div><p class="t-small dim">Score yourself. No pressure, <regex>user_name</regex>.</p></div>	<div class="card"><div class="card-title">Bread baking quiz</div><p class="muted">A few questions to see if you're proofing like a pro.</p><div class="quiz"><div class="q">1. What does a sourdough starter need to stay active?</div><details><summary>A) Regular feeding with flour and water</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Feed it regularly and keep it warm.</div></details><details><summary>B) Direct sunlight</summary></details><details><summary>C) A sealed jar in the fridge forever</summary></details></div><div class="divider"></div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">2. What is