23.31.0	quiz_question/Budgeting methods quiz	<div class="card"><div class="card-title">Budgeting methods quiz</div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">1. In the 50/30/20 rule, what does the 30% cover?</div><details><summary>A) Savings</summary></details><details><summary>B) Wants</summary><div class="answer">Correct. 50% needs, 30% wants, 20% savings/debt.</div></details><details><summary>C) Debt repayment</summary></details></div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">2. Which method gives every dollar a job before the month starts?</div><details><summary>A) Zero-based budgeting</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Zero-based means income minus outflows equals zero—nothing unassigned.</div></details><details><summary>B) Pay-yourself-first</summary></details><details><summary>C) Envelope system</summary></details></div><div class="callout good"><p class="t-small">No single method is perfect. <regex>user_name</regex>, the best budget is the one you'll actually check twice a month.</p></div></div>	<div class="card"><div class="card-title">Budgeting methods quiz</div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">1. In the 50/30/20 rule, what does the 30% cover?</div><details><summary>A) Savings</summary></details><details><summary>B) Wants</summary><div class="answer">Correct. 50% needs, 30% wants, 20% savings/debt.</div></details><details><summary>C) Debt repayment</summary></details></div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">2. Which method gives every dollar a job before the month starts?</div><details><summary>A) Zero-based budgeting</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Zero-based means income minus outflows equals zero—nothing unassigned.</div></details><details><summary>B) Pay-yourself-first</summary></details><details><summary>C) Envelope system</summary></details></div><div class="callout good"><p class="t-small">No single method is perfect. , the best budget is the one you'll actually check twice a month.</p></div></div>	-
23.32.0	quiz_question/Composting quiz	<div class="card"><div class="card-title">Composting quiz</div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">1. Which of these is a "green" (nitrogen-rich) compost material?</div><details><summary>A) Dry leaves</summary></details><details><summary>B) Coffee grounds</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Coffee grounds are greens. Dry leaves are browns (carbon-rich).</div></details><details><summary>C) Cardboard</summary></details></div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">2. What's the ideal ratio of browns to greens?</div><details><summary>A) 1:1</summary></details><details><summary>B) 3:1</summary></details><details><summary>C) 2:1 to 3:1 browns to greens</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Roughly 2–3 parts browns to 1 part greens keeps it from getting stinky.</div></details></div><div class="callout warn"><p class="t-small">Skip meat, dairy, and oily foods unless you've got a hot pile. <regex>user_name</regex>, they attract critters.</p></div></div>	<div class="card"><div class="card-title">Composting quiz</div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">1. Which of these is a "green" (nitrogen-rich) compost material?</div><details><summary>A) Dry leaves</summary></details><details><summary>B) Coffee grounds</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Coffee grounds are greens. Dry leaves are browns (carbon-rich).</div></details><details><summary>C) Cardboard</summary></details></div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">2. What's the ideal ratio of browns to greens?</div><details><summary>A) 1:1</summary></details><details><summary>B) 3:1</summary></details><details><summary>C) 2:1 to 3:1 browns to greens</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Roughly 2–3 parts browns to 1 part greens keeps it from getting stinky.</div></details></div><div class="callout warn"><p class="t-small">Skip meat, dairy, and oily foods unless you've got a hot pile. , they attract critters.</p></div></div>	-
