23.41.0	quiz_question/Basic electrical safety quiz	<div class="quiz"><div class="q">What should you do before working on an electrical circuit?</div><details><summary>A) Turn off the light switch</summary><div class="answer">Incorrect. The switch may not cut all power.</div></details><details><summary>B) Turn off the breaker and test for power</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Always verify the circuit is dead.</div></details><details><summary>C) Wear rubber gloves</summary><div class="answer">Incorrect. Gloves alone aren't enough.</div></details><details><summary>D) Work quickly to avoid shock</summary><div class="answer">Incorrect. Never rush electrical work.</div></details></div>	<div class="quiz"><div class="q">What should you do before working on an electrical circuit?</div><details><summary>A) Turn off the light switch</summary><div class="answer">Incorrect. The switch may not cut all power.</div></details><details><summary>B) Turn off the breaker and test for power</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Always verify the circuit is dead.</div></details><details><summary>C) Wear rubber gloves</summary><div class="answer">Incorrect. Gloves alone aren't enough.</div></details><details><summary>D) Work quickly to avoid shock</summary><div class="answer">Incorrect. Never rush electrical work.</div></details></div>	-
23.42.0	quiz_question/Tea basics quiz	<div class="card"><div class="card-title">Tea basics quiz for <regex>user_name</regex></div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">What water temperature is best for green tea?</div><details><summary>A) 100°C/212°F</summary><div class="answer">Too hot. That scorches green leaves and makes them bitter.</div></details><details><summary>B) 70–80°C/158–176°F</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Green tea likes it gentle. Let the kettle rest a minute after boiling.</div></details><details><summary>C) 60°C/140°F</summary><div class="answer">A bit low. That's closer to a delicate white tea. Green tea sits in the middle.</div></details></div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">How long should you steep black tea?</div><details><summary>A) 1 minute</summary><div class="answer">Too short. You'll get a weak, watery cup.</div></details><details><summary>B) 3–5 minutes</summary><div class="answer">Correct. That's the sweet spot for a robust black tea.</div></details><details><summary>C) 10 minutes</summary><div class="answer">Way too long. That's where the bitterness creeps in.</div></details></div><p class="muted">Two down. Your tea game is getting stronger.</p></div>	<div class="card"><div class="card-title">Tea basics quiz for </div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">What water temperature is best for green tea?</div><details><summary>A) 100°C/212°F</summary><div class="answer">Too hot. That scorches green leaves and makes them bitter.</div></details><details><summary>B) 70–80°C/158–176°F</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Green tea likes it gentle. Let the kettle rest a minute after boiling.</div></details><details><summary>C) 60°C/140°F</summary><div class="answer">A bit low. That's closer to a delicate white tea. Green tea sits in the middle.</div></details></div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">How long should you steep black tea?</div><details><summary>A) 1 minute</summary><div class="answer">Too short. You'll get a weak, watery cup.</div><