23.43.0	quiz_question/DIY wall painting quiz	<div class="card"><div class="card-title">DIY wall painting quiz for <regex>user_name</regex></div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">What should you do before painting a wall?</div><details><summary>A) Just start painting</summary><div class="answer">Not quite. Prep is half the job. Clean, patch, and tape first.</div></details><details><summary>B) Clean, patch holes, and tape edges</summary><div class="answer">Correct. A smooth surface makes the paint look professional.</div></details><details><summary>C) Only tape the edges</summary><div class="answer">Close, but you also need to clean and patch. Paint won't hide lumps.</div></details></div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">How many coats of paint are usually needed?</div><details><summary>A) One thick coat</summary><div class="answer">A single thick coat often looks uneven and can drip.</div></details><details><summary>B) Two thin coats</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Two thin coats give better coverage and a smoother finish.</div></details><details><summary>C) Five coats</summary><div class="answer">Overkill. Unless you're covering a very dark color, two is plenty.</div></details></div><p class="muted">Now grab a roller. You've got this.</p></div>	<div class="card"><div class="card-title">DIY wall painting quiz for </div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">What should you do before painting a wall?</div><details><summary>A) Just start painting</summary><div class="answer">Not quite. Prep is half the job. Clean, patch, and tape first.</div></details><details><summary>B) Clean, patch holes, and tape edges</summary><div class="answer">Correct. A smooth surface makes the paint look professional.</div></details><details><summary>C) Only tape the edges</summary><div class="answer">Close, but you also need to clean and patch. Paint won't hide lumps.</div></details></div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">How many coats of paint are usually needed?</div><details><summary>A) One thick coat</summary><div class="answer">A single thick coat often looks uneven and can drip.</div></details><details><summary>B) Two thin coats</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Two thin coats give better coverage and a smoother finish.</div></details><details><summary>C) Five coats</summary><div class="answer">Overkill. Unless you're covering a very dark color, two is plenty.</div></details></div><p class="muted">Now grab a roller. You've got this.</p></div>	-
23.44.0	quiz_question/Tire pressure quiz	<div class="card"><div class="card-title">Tire pressure quiz for <regex>user_name</regex></div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">How often should you check tire pressure?</div><details><summary>A) Once a year</summary><div class="answer">Too infrequent. Tires can lose pressure gradually, affecting safety and fuel economy.</div></details><details><summary>B) Once a month</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Monthly checks keep you safe and save fuel.</div></details><details><summary>C) Only when a tire looks flat</summary><div class="answer">By then it's already too low. Check regularly, not just when it's obvious.</div></details></div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">Where do you find the recommended tire pressure for your car?</div><details><summary>A) On the tire sidewall</summary><div class="answer">That's the maximum pressure, not the recommended one.</div></details><details><summary>B) In the owner's manual or driver's door jamb</summary><div class="answer">Correct. That's the manufacturer's recommendation for your specific car.</div></details><details><summary>C) Guess based on tire size</summary><div class="answer">Guessing is risky. Always check the manual or door jamb sticker.</div></details></div><p class="muted">A quick check now saves a blowout later.</p></div>	<div class="card"><div class="card-title">Tire pressure quiz for </div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">How often should you check tire pressure?</div><details><summary>A) Once a year</summary><div class="answer">Too infrequent. Tires can lose pressure gradually, affecting safety and fuel economy.</div></details><details><summary>B) Once a month</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Monthly checks keep you safe and save fuel.</div></details><details><summary>C) Only when a tire looks flat</summary><div class="answer">By then it's already too low. Check regularly, not just when it's obvious.</div></details></div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">Where do you 