23.54.0	quiz_question/Basic car tire changing quiz	<div class="umi-page"><div class="card"><div class="card-title">Changing a flat tire</div><p class="muted">Ready, <regex>user_name</regex>? Pick the best answer.</p><div class="quiz"><div class="q">What should you do first when you get a flat?</div><details><summary>A) Jack up the car</summary></details><details><summary>B) Loosen the lug nuts slightly</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Loosen them a quarter-turn while the tire is still on the ground — it's much harder once it's in the air.</div></details><details><summary>C) Call a tow truck</summary></details></div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">Where is the safest place to put the jack?</div><details><summary>A) Under the bumper</summary></details><details><summary>B) On the pinch weld or jack point</summary><div class="answer">Right. Check your manual for the exact jack points — usually a reinforced seam or notch.</div></details><details><summary>C) Under the door</summary></details></div><div class="callout warn">Never crawl under a car supported only by a jack. Use jack stands.</div></div></div>	<div class="umi-page"><div class="card"><div class="card-title">Changing a flat tire</div><p class="muted">Ready, ? Pick the best answer.</p><div class="quiz"><div class="q">What should you do first when you get a flat?</div><details><summary>A) Jack up the car</summary></details><details><summary>B) Loosen the lug nuts slightly</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Loosen them a quarter-turn while the tire is still on the ground — it's much harder once it's in the air.</div></details><details><summary>C) Call a tow truck</summary></details></div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">Where is the safest place to put the jack?</div><details><summary>A) Under the bumper</summary></details><details><summary>B) On the pinch weld or jack point</summary><div class="answer">Right. Check your manual for the exact jack points — usually a reinforced seam or notch.</div></details