23.5.1	quiz_question/Basic bike chain care quiz	<div class="quiz"><div class="q">Ready, <regex>user_name</regex>? One question on keeping a bike chain happy.</div><details><summary>A) A chain should run bone dry to avoid dirt sticking</summary></details><details><summary>B) Wipe off old lube, apply fresh, then wipe the excess</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Clean first, lube lightly, wipe again. Excess lube is just a dirt magnet waiting to happen.</div></details><details><summary>C) Any oil from the kitchen works fine</summary></details><details><summary>D) Chains never need attention until they snap</summary></details></div>	<div class="quiz"><div class="q">Ready, ? One question on keeping a bike chain happy.</div><details><summary>A) A chain should run bone dry to avoid dirt sticking</summary></details><details><summary>B) Wipe off old lube, apply fresh, then wipe the excess</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Clean first, lube lightly, wipe again. Excess lube is just a dirt magnet waiting to happen.</div></details><details><summary>C) Any oil from the kitchen works fine</summary></details><details><summary>D) Chains never need attention until they snap</summary></details></div>	-
23.6.1	quiz_question/Basic bicycle inner tube repair quiz	<div class="quiz"><div class="q">Flat tyre, <regex>user_name</regex>? Let's see if you'd get home.</div><details><summary>A) Glue the patch straight onto a dusty tube</summary></details><details><summary>B) Rough up the area, wait for glue to go tacky, then press the patch on</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Scuff, glue, wait until it's dry to the touch, then press firmly and hold. Dust is the enemy of a good bond.</div></details><details><summary>C) Skip the glue, the patch sticks on its own</summary></details><details><summary>D) Inflate hard immediately to set the patch</summary></details></div>	<div class="quiz"><div class="q">Flat tyre, ? Let's see if you'd get home.</div><details><summary>A) Glue the patch straight onto a dusty tube</summary></details><details><summary>B) Rough up the area, wait for glue to go tacky, then press the patch on</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Scuff, glue, wait until it's dry to the touch, then press firmly and hold. Dust is the enemy of a good bond.</div></details><details><summary>C) Skip the glue, the patch sticks on its own</summary></details><details><summary>D) Inflate hard immediately to set the patch</summary></details></div>	-
23.7.1	quiz_question/Basic shoe care quiz	<div class="quiz"><div class="q">Nice shoes, <regex>user_name</regex>. Let's keep them that way.</div><details><summary>A) Dry wet leather shoes on a radiator for speed</summary></details><details><summary>B) Air dry away from direct heat, then condition</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Heat cracks leather. Stuff them with newspaper, let them dry slowly, then feed the leather.</div></details><details><summary>C) Wash leather in the machine on cold</summary></details><details><summary>D) Never clean them, it wears them out</summary></details></div>	<div class="quiz"><div class="q">Nice shoes, . Let's keep them that way.</div><details><summary>A) Dry wet leather shoes on a radiator for speed</summary></details><details><summary>B) Air dry away from direct heat, then condition</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Heat cracks leather. Stuff them with newspaper, let them dry slowly, then feed the leather.</div></details><details><summary>C) Wash leather in the machine on cold</summary></details><details><summary>D) Never clean them, it wears them out</summary></details></div>	-
23.8.1	quiz_question/Basic refrigerator food storage quiz	<div class="quiz"><div class="q">Quick one, <regex>user_name</regex>: which shelf keeps food safest?</div><details><summary>A) Raw meat on the top shelf, for easy reach</summary></details><details><summary>B) Raw meat on the bottom shelf, in a sealed container</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Bottom shelf means any drips can't rain onto ready-to-eat food below. The door is the warmest spot, so keep milk out of it.</div></details><details><summary>C) Everything in the door, it's handiest</summary></details><details><summary>D) Eggs belong in the freezer</summary></details></div>	<div class="quiz"><div class="q">Quick one, : which shelf keeps food safest?</div><details><summary>A) Raw meat on the top shelf, for easy reach</summary></details><details><summary>B) Raw meat on the bottom shelf, in a sealed container</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Bottom shelf means any drips can't rain onto ready-to-eat food below. The door is the warmest spot, so keep milk out of it.</div></details><details><summary>C) Everything in the door, it's handiest</summary></details><details><summary>D) Eggs belong in the freezer</summary></details></div>	-
23.9.1	quiz_question/Basic window cleaning quiz	<div class="quiz"><div class="q">Squeaky clean, <regex>user_name</regex>? Let's check your technique.</div><details><summary>A) Scrub in circles in full sun, then let it dry</summary></details><details><summary>B) Wash, squeegee in overlapping strokes, wipe the blade between passes</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Work out of direct sun, pull the squeegee in a top-to-bottom zigzag, and dry the blade each time. Streaks come from dirty blades and midday heat.</div></details><details><summary>C) Newspaper and spit, always</summary></details><details><summary>D) More soap means fewer streaks</summary></details></div>	<div class="quiz"><div class="q">Squeaky clean, ? Let's check your technique.</div><details><summary>A) Scrub in circles in full sun, then let it dry</summary></details><details><summary>B) Wash, squeegee in overlapping strokes, wipe the blade between passes</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Work out of direct sun, pull the squeegee in a top-to-bottom zigzag, and dry the blade each time. Streaks come from dirty blades and midday heat.</div></details><details><summary>C) Newspaper and spit, always</summary></details><details><summary>D) More soap means fewer streaks</summary></details></div>	-
23.10.1	quiz_question/Basic houseplant watering quiz	<div class="quiz"><div class="q">Plant parent check, <regex>user_name</regex>. When do you water?</div><details><summary>A) On a strict weekly schedule come what may</summary></details><details><summary>B) When the top few centimetres of soil feel dry to your finger</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Stick a finger in, not a calendar. Light, season and pot size all change the answer, and soggy roots kill more plants than thirst.</div></details><details><summary>C) A little every single day</summary></details><details><summary>D) Only when the leaves go brown and crispy</summary></details></div>	<div class="quiz"><div class="q">Plant parent check, . When do you water?</div><details><summary>A) On a strict weekly schedule come what may</summary></details><details><summary>B) When the top few centimetres of soil feel dry to your finger</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Stick a finger in, not a calendar. Light, season and pot size all change the answer, and soggy roots kill more plants than thirst.</div></details><details><summary>C) A little every single day</summary></details><details><summary>D) Only when the leaves go brown and crispy</summary></details></div>	-
23.11.1	quiz_question/Basic laundry quiz	<div class="quiz"><div class="q">Washing whites with hot water is best for:</div><details><summary>A) Keeping colors bright</summary></details><details><summary>B) Removing stains and sanitizing</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Hot water helps lift stains and kill germs, but can fade colors and shrink some fabrics.</div></details><details><summary>C) Saving energy</summary></details></div><p class="muted">Next time you sort, check the care label first. It knows more than we do.</p>	<div class="quiz"><div class="q">Washing whites with hot water is best for:</div><details><summary>A) Keeping colors bright</summary></details><details><summary>B) Removing stains and sanitizing</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Hot water helps lift stains and kill germs, but can fade colors and shrink some fabrics.</div></details><details><summary>C) Saving energy</summary></details></div><p class="muted">Next time you sort, check the care label first. It knows more than we do.</p>	-
23.12.1	quiz_question/Basic plant propagation quiz	<div class="quiz"><div class="q">When rooting a pothos cutting in water, where should the leaf node be?</div><details><summary>A) Above the water line</summary></details><details><summary>B) Submerged in the water</summary><div class="answer">Correct. The node (where roots emerge) must be underwater. Leaves above the water line prevent rot.</div></details><details><summary>C) Doesn't matter</summary></details></div><p class="muted">Change the water weekly. Roots like fresh oxygen.</p>	<div class="quiz"><div class="q">When rooting a pothos cutting in water, where should the leaf node be?</div><details><summary>A) Above the water line</summary></details><details><summary>B) Submerged in the water</summary><div class="answer">Correct. The node (where roots emerge) must be underwater. Leaves above the water line prevent rot.</div></details><details><summary>C) Doesn't matter</summary></details></div><p class="muted">Change the water weekly. Roots like fresh oxygen.</p>	-
23.13.1	quiz_question/Basic necktie knot quiz	<div class="quiz"><div class="q">Which tie knot is generally the simplest and most versatile?</div><details><summary>A) Windsor</summary></details><details><summary>B) Four-in-hand</summary><div class="answer">Correct. The four-in-hand is slim, easy, and works with most collars and ties.</div></details><details><summary>C) Pratt</summary></details></div><p class="muted">If you can tie your shoes, you can tie a four-in-hand. Give it a try.</p>	<div class="quiz"><div class="q">Which tie knot is generally the simplest and most versatile?</div><details><summary>A) Windsor</summary></details><details><summary>B) Four-in-hand</summary><div class="answer">Correct. The four-in-hand is slim, easy, and works with most collars and ties.</div></details><details><summary>C) Pratt</summary></details></div><p class="muted">If you can tie your shoes, you can tie a four-in-hand. Give it a try.</p>	-
23.14.1	quiz_question/Basic bike tire repair quiz	<div class="quiz"><div class="q">Before patching a punctured inner tube, what should you do first?</div><details><summary>A) Inflate it to find the leak</summary><div class="answer">Correct. A little air helps you hear or feel the escaping air and locate the hole.</div></details><details><summary>B) Glue the patch immediately</summary></details><details><summary>C) Throw it away</summary></details></div><p class="muted">Rough up the area, apply glue, wait a minute, then press the patch. Patience pays.</p>	<div class="quiz"><div class="q">Before patching a punctured inner tube, what should you do first?</div><details><summary>A) Inflate it to find the leak</summary><div class="answer">Correct. A little air helps you hear or feel the escaping air and locate the hole.</div></details><details><summary>B) Glue the patch immediately</summary></details><details><summary>C) Throw it away</summary></details></div><p class="muted">Rough up the area, apply glue, wait a minute, then press the patch. Patience pays.</p>	-
23.15.1	quiz_question/Basic coffee grind size quiz	<div class="quiz"><div class="q">Which brewing method needs the coarsest grind?</div><details><summary>A) Espresso</summary></details><details><summary>B) French press</summary><div class="answer">Correct. French press uses a coarse grind so the metal filter can catch the grounds.</div></details><details><summary>C) Drip</summary></details></div><p class="muted">Grind fresh if you can. It makes a bigger difference than you'd think.</p>	<div class="quiz"><div class="q">Which brewing method needs the coarsest grind?</div><details><summary>A) Espresso</summary></details><details><summary>B) French press</summary><div class="answer">Correct. French press uses a coarse grind so the metal filter can catch the grounds.</div></details><details><summary>C) Drip</summary></details></div><p class="muted">Grind fresh if you can. It makes a bigger difference than you'd think.</p>	-
23.16.1	quiz_question/Basic car fluid check quiz	<div class="quiz"><div class="q">When checking engine oil with the dipstick, the engine should be:</div><details><summary>A) Running</summary></details><details><summary>B) Off and cool</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Turn off the engine, wait a few minutes, then check. Hot oil can burn you.</div></details><details><summary>C) Hot but off</summary></details></div><p class="muted">Wipe, dip, wipe, dip again. The second reading is the honest one.</p>	<div class="quiz"><div class="q">When checking engine oil with the dipstick, the engine should be:</div><details><summary>A) Running</summary></details><details><summary>B) Off and cool</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Turn off the engine, wait a few minutes, then check. Hot oil can burn you.</div></details><details><summary>C) Hot but off</summary></details></div><p class="muted">Wipe, dip, wipe, dip again. The second reading is the honest one.</p>	-
23.17.1	quiz_question/Basic smoke alarm care quiz	<div class="umi-page"><div class="stack"><p class="muted t-small">Alright <regex>user_name</regex>, four questions on keeping that little circle on the ceiling alive.</p><div class="quiz"><div class="q">1. How often should you press the test button?</div><details><summary>A) Once a year</summary></details><details><summary>B) Once a month</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Monthly press, yearly deep clean, replace the unit every 10 years.</div></details><details><summary>C) Only when it chirps</summary></details></div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">2. The alarm chirps every 30-60 seconds. What does that mean?</div><details><summary>A) It is broken, buy a new one</summary></details><details><summary>B) Low battery warning</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Swap the battery now, do not wait for a full beep.</div></details><details><summary>C) Dust in the sensor</summary></details></div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">3. Best way to clean it?</div><details><summary>A) Vacuum the vents, wipe the case</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Soft brush or vacuum nozzle, never water or spray cleaner inside.</div></details><details><summary>B) Run it under the tap</summary></details><details><summary>C) Blow into the sensor hole</summary></details></div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">4. Where does it belong?</div><details><summary>A) Near the kitchen stove</summary></details><details><summary>B) On the ceiling, away from vents and windows</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Keep it at least 3 m from cooking fumes and out of dead-air corners.</div></details><details><summary>C) In the basement only</summary></details></div><p class="muted t-small">Nice. One press of a button is a small thing that buys you a lot.</p></div></div>	<div class="umi-page"><div class="stack"><p class="muted t-small">Alright , four questions on keeping that little circle on the ceiling alive.</p><div class="quiz"><div class="q">1. How ofte