23.18.1	quiz_question/Basic dishwashing by hand quiz	<div class="umi-page"><div class="stack"><p class="muted t-small">Hey <regex>user_name</regex>. Three questions on the sink end of things.</p><div class="quiz"><div class="q">1. What order should you wash in?</div><details><summary>A) Whatever is closest</summary></details><details><summary>B) Cleanest first: glasses, then plates, then pots</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Grease travels downward, so keep the light stuff out of the way first.</div></details><details><summary>C) Pots first, they need the hottest water</summary></details></div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">2. Best water temperature for hand washing?</div><details><summary>A) Cold, to save energy</summary></details><details><summary>B) As hot as your hands can stand</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Around 45-50 degrees C loosens grease without scalding you.</div></details><details><summary>C) Lukewarm is fine</summary></details></div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">3. Sponge looking sad and smelling odd. What now?</div><details><summary>A) Keep using it, it still works</summary></details><details><summary>B) Replace it, or microwave a damp one for one minute</summary><div class="answer">Correct. A damp sponge in the microwave for 60 seconds is a decent reset. Replace weekly anyway.</div></details><details><summary>C) Rinse it in cold water</summary></details></div><p class="muted t-small">Good. Your glasses will thank you.</p></div></div>	<div class="umi-page"><div class="stack"><p class="muted t-small">Hey . Three questions on the sink end of things.</p><div class="quiz"><div class="q">1. What order should you wash in?</div><details><summary>A) Whatever is closest</summary></details><details><summary>B) Cleanest first: glasses, then plates, then pots</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Grease travels downward, so keep the light stuff out of the way first.</div></details><details><summary>C) Pots first, they need the hottest water</summary></details></div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">2. Best water temperature for hand washing?</div><details><summary>A) Cold, to save energy</summary></details><details><summary>B) As hot as your hands can stand</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Around 45-50 degrees C loosens grease without scalding you.</div></details><details><summary>C) Lukewarm is fine</summary></details></div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">3. Sponge looking sad and smelling odd. What now?</div><details><summary>A) Keep using it, it still works</summary></details><details><summary>B) Replace it, or microwave a damp one for one minute</summary><div class="answer">Correct. A damp sponge in the microwave for 60 seconds is a decent reset. Replace weekly anyway.</div></details><details><summary>C) Rinse it in cold water</summary></details></div><p class="muted t-small">Good. Your glasses will thank you.</p></div></div>	-
23.19.1	quiz_question/Basic charcoal grilling quiz	<div class="umi-page"><div class="stack"><p class="muted t-small">Evening, <regex>user_name</regex>. Four quick ones on the kettle grill.</p><div class="quiz"><div class="q">1. How full should a chimney starter be?</div><details><summary>A) Packed to the rim</summary></details><details><summary>B) About three-quarters full</summary><div class="answer">Correct. A full chimney is a lot of heat. Three-quarters is plenty for a family cook.</div></details><details><summary>C) One small handful</summary></details></div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">2. When are the coals ready?</div><details><summary>A) When flames appear</summary></details><details><summary>B) When they are grey with ash and glowing underneath</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Flames mean it is still too hot and still burning off lighter fluid.</div></details><details><summary>C) Twenty seconds after lighting</summary></details></div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">3. Two-zone setup: what is it for?</div><details><summary>A) Direct heat on one side, no coals on the other</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Sear over the coals, finish on the cool side. It is also your escape hatch for flare-ups.</div></details><details><summary>B) Two piles, one at each end</summary></details><details><summary>C) Coals under a water pan</summary></details></div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">4. How do you tame a flare-up?</div><details><summary>A) Close the lid and the vents</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Starve it of air. Move food to the cool zone and let it settle.</div></details><details><summary>B) Squirt water on the coals</summary></details><details><summary>C) Spread the coals out</summary></details></div><p class="muted t-small">Good luck out there. Smoke is a feature, not a bug.</p></div></div>	<div class="umi-page"><div class="stack"><p class="muted t-small">Evening, . Four quick ones on the kettle grill.</p><div class="quiz"><div class="q">1. How full should a chimney starter be?</div><details><summary>A) Packed to the rim</summary></details><details><summary>B) About three-quarters full</summary><div class="answer">Correct. A full chimney is a lot of heat. Three-quarters is plenty for a family cook.</div></details><details><summary>C) One small handful</summary></details></div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">2. When are the coals ready?</div><details><summary>A) When flames appear</summary></details><details><summary>B) When they are grey with ash and glowing underneath</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Flames mean it is still too hot and still burning off lighter fluid.</div></details><details><summary>C) Twenty seconds after lighting</summary></details></div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">3. Two-zone setup: what is it for?</div><details><summary>A) Direct heat on one side, no coals on the other</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Sear over the coals, finish on the cool side. It is also your escape hatch for flare-ups.</div></details><details><summary>B) Two piles, one at each end</summary></details><details><summary>C) Coals under a water pan</summary></details></div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">4. How do you tame a flare-up?</div><details><summary>A) Close the lid and the vents</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Starve it of air. Move food to the cool zone and let it settle.</div></details><details><summary>B) Squirt water on the coals</summary></details><details><summary>C) Spread the coals out</summary></details></div><p class="muted t-small">Good luck out there. Smoke is a feature, not a bug.</p></div></div>	-
23.20.1	quiz_question/Basic clothing stain removal quiz	<div class="umi-page"><div class="stack"><p class="muted t-small">Hi <regex>user_name</regex>. Four stains, four answers. Blot first, always.</p><div class="quiz"><div class="q">1. First move when coffee hits your shirt?</div><details><summary>A) Rub it in with soap</summary></details><details><summary>B) Blot from the back with cold water</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Rubbing spreads the stain and pushes it into the fibres.</div></details><details><summary>C) Reach for hot water</summary></details></div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">2. Blood stain, fresh. Water temperature?</div><details><summary>A) Cold</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Hot water sets the protein. Cold water and a little soap, then wash as normal.</div></details><details><summary>B) Hot</summary></details><details><summary>C) Boiling</summary></details></div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">3. Grease mark on a cotton shirt. What helps most?</div><details><summary>A) Dish soap worked in with your fingers</summary><div class="answer">Correct. A drop of dish soap, gentle rub, then wash. Baking soda on top helps for tough spots.</div></details><details><summary>B) More oil</summary></details><details><summary>C) Hairspray</summary></details></div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">4. Grass stain, stubborn. What do you reach for?</div><details><summary>A) White vinegar or an enzyme detergent</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Soak 15 minutes, then wash on the warmest setting the label allows.</div></details><details><summary>B) Bleach on everything</summary></details><details><summary>C) Just hope it fades</summary></details></div><p class="muted t-small">Good. Now go rescue that shirt.</p></div></div>	<div class="umi-page"><div class="stack"><p class="muted t-small">Hi . Four stains, four answers. Blot first, always.</p><div class="quiz"><div class="q">1. First move when coffee hits your shirt?</div><details><summary>A) Rub it in 