23.21.1	quiz_question/Basic resume layout quiz	<div class="umi-page"><div class="stack"><p class="muted t-small">Right <regex>user_name</regex>, three questions on the document that gets you the interview.</p><div class="quiz"><div class="q">1. Best length for most people with under 10 years experience?</div><details><summary>A) One page</summary><div class="answer">Correct. One page unless you have real depth to show. Two pages is fine later, not now.</div></details><details><summary>B) Three pages minimum</summary></details><details><summary>C) As long as it needs to be</summary></details></div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">2. Which bullet is stronger?</div><details><summary>A) "Responsible for social media"</summary></details><details><summary>B) "Grew newsletter from 400 to 2,100 subscribers in six months"</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Numbers, verbs, outcomes. Vague duties tell a recruiter nothing.</div></details><details><summary>C) "Team player with great attitude"</summary></details></div><div class="quiz"><div class="q">3. What should be the very top line?</div><details><summary>A) Objective statement</summary></details><details><summary>B) Your name, phone, email, one link</summary><div class="answer">Correct. Make it easy to contact you in the first two seconds.</div></details><details><summary>C) A photo</summary></details></div><p class="muted t-small">Nice. One page, one focus, one clear ask.</p></div></div>	<div class="umi-page"><div class="stack"><p class="muted t-small">Right , three questions on the document that gets you the interview.</p><div class="quiz"><div class="q">1. Best length for most people with under 10 years experience?</div><details><summary>A) One page</summary><div class="answer">Correct. One page unless you have real depth to show. Two pages is fine later, not now.</div></details><details><summary>B) Three pages minimum</summary></details><details><summary>C) As long as it needs to be</summary></details></div><div class