24.39.0	glossary/Film Photography Glossary	<div class="card"><h4>Film Photography Glossary</h4><p class="muted t-small">Your lab slip decoded, <regex>user_name</regex>.</p><ul class="list"><li><b>Stop</b> — a doubling or halving of light. One stop brighter, one stop dimmer.</li><li><b>Push processing</b> — developing as if the film were faster, to gain shadow detail. Costs contrast and grain.</li><li><b>Pull processing</b> — the opposite; gentler contrast, thinner negatives.</li><li><b>Latitude</b> — how much over- or under-exposure a film forgives. Negative film is generous; slide film is not.</li><li><b>Grain</b> — clumps of developed silver. Not the same as digital noise, even when it looks similar.</li><li><b>Bracketing</b> — shooting the same frame at different exposures, hoping one lands.</li><li><b>C-41 / E-6</b> — standard colour development for negatives / for slides.</li></ul><div class="callout good"><p class="t-small">Overexpose negative film slightly. It's the closest thing to a cheat code.</p></div></div>	<div class="card"><h4>Film Photography Glossary</h4><p class="muted t-small">Your lab slip decoded, .</p><ul class="list"><li><b>Stop</b> — a doubling or halving of light. One stop brighter, one stop dimmer.</li><li><b>Push processing</b> — developing as if the film were faster, to gain shadow detail. Costs contrast and grain.</li><li><b>Pull processing</b> — the opposite; gentler contrast, thinner negatives.</li><li><b>Latitude</b> — how much over- or under-exposure a film forgives. Negative film is generous; slide film is not.</li><li><b>Grain</b> — clumps of developed silver. Not the same as digital noise, even when it looks similar.</li><li><b>Bracketing</b> — shooting the same frame at different exposures, hoping one lands.</li><li><b>C-41 / E-6</b> — standard colour development for negatives / for slides.</li></ul><div class="callout good"><p class="t-small">Overexpose negative film slightly. It's the closest thing to a cheat code.</p></div></di