24.1.1	glossary/Chess Board Geometry Glossary	<div class="card"><h4>Chess Board Geometry</h4><p class="muted">Files, ranks, and the invisible lines that decide games, <regex>user_name</regex>.</p><ul class="list"><li><b>File</b> — a column, named a through h. Vertical.</li><li><b>Rank</b> — a row, numbered 1 through 8. Horizontal.</li><li><b>Diagonal</b> — the bishop's playground, all one colour.</li><li><b>Centre</b> — d4, d5, e4, e5. The prime real estate.</li><li><b>Squares in the corner</b> — a1 and h8 are dark; a8 and h1 are light. "Light on the right" for the h1 corner.</li><li><b>Open file</b> — no pawns left on it. Rooks love these.</li><li><b>Half-open file</b> — only your opponent has a pawn there.</li></ul><details class="acc"><summary>Why the centre matters</summary><div class="body"><p>A piece in the middle reaches more squares. From e4, a knight touches eight; from a1, only two.</p></div></details><div class="callout info">Name a square out loud and everyone at the board knows exactly where you mean.</div></div>	<div class="card"><h4>Chess Board Geometry</h4><p class="muted">Files, ranks, and the invisible lines that decide games, .</p><ul class="list"><li><b>File</b> — a column, named a through h. Vertical.</li><li><b>Rank</b> — a row, numbered 1 through 8. Horizontal.</li><li><b>Diagonal</b> — the bishop's playground, all one colour.</li><li><b>Centre</b> — d4, d5, e4, e5. The prime real estate.</li><li><b>Squares in the corner</b> — a1 and h8 are dark; a8 and h1 are light. "Light on the right" for the h1 corner.</li><li><b>Open file</b> — no pawns left on it. Rooks love these.</li><li><b>Half-open file</b> — only your opponent has a pawn there.</li></ul><details class="acc"><summary>Why the centre matters</summary><div class="body"><p>A piece in the middle reaches more squares. From e4, a knight touches eight; from a1, only two.</p></div></details><div class="callout info">Name a square out loud and everyone at the board knows exactly where you mean