26.2.0	checklist/Job interview prep checklist	<div class="card">  <h4 class="card-title">Interview prep</h4>  <p class="muted t-small">Do these once, then rest, <regex>user_name</regex>.</p>  <ul class="list">    <li>Re-read the job ad; highlight the three things they repeat</li>    <li>Match each one to a story you can tell in 90 seconds</li>    <li>Look up the interviewer and the team's recent work</li>    <li>Prepare two questions <em>you</em> want answered</li>    <li>Plan the route, or test the video link a day early</li>    <li>Lay out clothes and print a spare copy of your CV</li>    <li>Sleep. Turn up curious, not perfect</li>  </ul>  <div class="callout good">"Tell me about yourself" is just the warm-up. Keep it to a minute.</div></div>	<div class="card">  <h4 class="card-title">Interview prep</h4>  <p class="muted t-small">Do these once, then rest, .</p>  <ul class="list">    <li>Re-read the job ad; highlight the three things they repeat</li>    <li>Match each one to a story you can tell in 90 seconds</li>    <li>Look up the interviewer and the team's recent work</li>    <li>Prepare two questions <em>you</em> want answered</li>    <li>Plan the route, or test the video link a day early</li>    <li>Lay out clothes and print a spare copy of your CV</li>    <li>Sleep. Turn up curious, not perfect</li>  </ul>  <div class="callout good">"Tell me about yourself" is just the warm-up. Keep it to a minute.</div></div>	-
26.3.0	checklist/Winter car readiness checklist	<div class="card">  <h4 class="card-title">Winter car check</h4>  <p class="muted t-small">Ten minutes now saves a cold hour later, <regex>user_name</regex>.</p>  <ul class="list">    <li>Tyre tread: at least 3mm, and check pressures cold</li>    <li>Antifreeze strength and screen-wash rated below freezing</li>    <li>Battery health — cold mornings are where old ones die</li>    <li>Wipers and all lights working</li>    <li>Keep an ice scraper, de-icer and a torch inside the car</li>    <li>Blanket, gloves, and a charged power bank in the boot</li>    <li>Top up fuel before it dips below a quarter tank</li>  </ul>  <details class="acc">    <summary>If you get stuck</summary>    <div class="body"><p class="muted">Stay with the car, keep the exhaust clear of snow, and run the engine in short bursts.</p></div>  </details></div>	<div class="card">  <h4 class="card-title">Winter car check</h4>  <p class="muted t-small">Ten minutes now saves a cold hour later, .</p>  <ul class="list">    <li>Tyre tread: at least 3mm, and check pressures cold</li>    <li>Antifreeze strength and screen-wash rated below freezing</li>    <li>Battery health — cold mornings are where old ones die</li>    <li>Wipers and all lights working</li>    <li>Keep an ice scraper, de-icer and a torch inside the car</li>    <li>Blanket, gloves, and a charged power bank in the boot</li>    <li>Top up fuel before it dips below a quarter tank</li>  </ul>  <details class="acc">    <summary>If you get stuck</summary>    <div class="body"><p class="muted">Stay with the car, keep the exhaust clear of snow, and run the engine in short bursts.</p></div>  </details></div>	-
26.4.0	checklist/Monthly money admin checklist	<div class="card">  <h4 class="card-title">Monthly money tidy</h4>  <p class="muted t-small">Fifteen minutes, once a month, <regex>user_name</regex>.</p>  <ul class="list">    <li>Check last month's spending against your rough budget</li>    <li>Move anything spare into savings, even a little</li>    <li>Review subscriptions — cancel one you forgot about</li>    <li>Pay the card that costs you most interest first</li>    <li>Log in and skim statements for odd charges</li>    <li>Confirm upcoming bills won't land before payday</li>  </ul>  <div class="callout warn">A budget you never look at is just a wish. Skim it monthly.</div></div>	<div class="card">  <h4 class="card-title">Monthly money tidy</h4>  <p class="muted t-small">Fifteen minutes, once a month, .</p>  <ul class="list">    <li>Check last month's spending against your rough budget</li>    <li>Move anything spare into savings, even a little</li>    <li>Review subscriptions — cancel one you forgot about</li>    <li>Pay the card that costs you most interest first</li>    <li>Log in and skim statements for odd charges</li>    <li>Confirm upcoming bills won't land before payday</li>  </ul>  <div class="callout warn">A budget you never look at is just a wish. Skim it monthly.</div></div>	-
26.5.0	checklist/Kitchen deep-clean checklist	<div class="card">  <h4 class="card-title">Kitchen deep clean</h4>  <p class="muted t-small">Top to bottom, so dirt falls onto what you've already done, <regex>user_name</regex>.</p>  <ol class="list">    <li>Clear counters and soak the hob grates in hot water</li>    <li>Dust the tops of cupboards and the extractor filter</li>    <li>Wipe cupboard doors, handles and light switches</li>    <li>Spray the hob, leave it a minute, then scrub</li>    <li>Pull out the fridge, clean behind it, then the shelves inside</li>    <li>Run a hot cycle through the dishwasher or drain</li>    <li>Mop the floor last, corners included</li>  </ol>  <details class="acc">    <summary>Order matters</summary>    <div class="body"><p class="muted">Any time you clean a wall, clean upward. Gravity is not on your side.</p></div>  </details></div>	<div class="card">  <h4 class="card-title">Kitchen deep clean</h4>  <p class="muted t-small">Top to bottom, so dirt falls onto what you've already done, .</p>  <ol class="list">    <li>Clear counters and soak the hob grates in hot water</li>    <li>Dust the tops of cupboards and the extractor filter</li>    <li>Wipe cupboard doors, handles and light switches</li>    <li>Spray the hob, leave it a minute, then scrub</li>    <li>Pull out the fridge, clean behind it, then the shelves inside</li>    <li>Run a hot cycle through the dishwasher or drain</li>    <li>Mop the floor last, corners included</li>  </ol>  <details class="acc">    <summary>Order matters</summary>    <div class="body"><p class="muted">Any time you clean a wall, clean upward. Gravity is not on your side.</p></div>  </details></div>	-
26.6.0	checklist/Camping trip gear checklist	<div class="card">  <h4 class="card-title">Camping trip gear — 2 nights, one car</h4>  <p class="muted t-small">Pack by pile: sleep, cook, wear, fix. Lay it all out first, then load.</p>  <ul class="list">    <li>Tent, poles, pegs <span class="badge good"><i class="dot"></i>check poles</span></li>    <li>Sleeping bag + mat (rated for the low, not the average)</li>    <li>Head torch, plus a spare set of batteries</li>    <li>Stove, fuel, lighter that actually sparks</li>    <li>Pot, mug, spork, small bottle of washing-up liquid</li>    <li>Water — 2 litres per person per day, filled before you leave</li>    <li>Food in one box: porridge, pasta, snacks, coffee</li>    <li>Layers: fleece, rain shell, dry socks, beanie</li>    <li>Boots broken in, sandals for the tent door</li>    <li>Bin bags (rubbish + wet clothes), kitchen roll, tape</li>    <li>First aid: plasters, painkillers, tick tweezers, antihistamine</li>    <li>Power bank, charged the night before</li>  </ul>  <details class="acc">    <summary>Things people forget</summary>    <div class="body">      <ul class="list">        <li>Pillow — a stuff sack of clothes works</li>        <li>Mallet for stubborn pegs, or a flat rock</li>        <li>Cash for the honesty box at the farm gate</li>      </ul>    </div>  </details>  <div class="callout info">Tents get cold at 3am. One extra layer beats one extra gadget, <regex>user_name</regex>.</div></div>	<div class="card">  <h4 class="card-title">Camping trip gear — 2 nights, one car</h4>  <p class="muted t-small">Pack by pile: sleep, cook, wear, fix. Lay it all out first, then load.</p>  <ul class="list">    <li>Tent, poles, pegs <span class="badge good"><i class="dot"></i>check poles</span></li>    <li>Sleeping bag + mat (rated for the low, not the average)</li>    <li>Head torch, plus a spare set of batteries</li>    <li>Stove, fuel, lighter that actually sparks</li>    <li>Pot, mug, spork, small bottle of washing-up liquid</li>    <li>Water — 2 litres per person per day, filled before you leave</li>    <li>Food in one box: porridge, pasta, snacks, coffee</li>    <li>Layers: fleece, rain shell, dry socks, beanie</li>    <li>Boots broken in, sandals for the tent door</li>    <li>Bin bags (rubbish + wet clothes), kitchen roll, tape</li>    <li>First aid: plasters, painkillers, tick tweezers, antihistamine</li>    <li>Power bank, charged the night before</li>  </ul>  <details class="acc">    <summary>Things people forget</summary>    <div class="body">      <ul class="list">        <li>Pillow — a stuff sack of clothes works</li>        <li>Mallet for stubborn pegs, or a flat rock</li>        <li>Cash for the honesty box at the farm gate</li>      </ul>    </div>  </details>  <div class="callout info">Tents get cold at 3am. One extra layer beats one extra gadget, .</div></div>	-
26.7.0	checklist/New puppy first week checklist	<div class="card">  <h4 class="card-title">New puppy — the first week</h4>  <p class="muted t-small">Buy less than you think. The first week is mostly routine and towels.</p>  <ul class="list">    <li>Same food the breeder was feeding — swap brands slowly over 7 days</li>    <li>Crate or bed in a quiet corner, not the busiest room</li>    <li>Collar + tag, and a lead you can hold with one hand</li>    <li>Two bowls, one for water that stays full</li>    <li>Enzyme cleaner for accidents — normal cleaner leaves the scent mark</li>    <li>Old towels by the door for wet paws</li>    <li>Chew toy and a soft toy. Not your slippers.</li>  </ul>  <div class="divider"></div>  <p class="muted t-small"><strong>First 48 hours</strong></p>  <ol class="list">    <li>Let the pup explore one room. No crowds of visitors.</li>    <li>Vet booked within 3 days for a check + vaccination plan.</li>    <li>Out to toilet every 90 minutes, and after every nap, meal, play.</li>    <li>Praise the second it finishes outside. Ten seconds late and it means nothing to them.</li>  </ol>  <div class="callout warn">No dog parks until the vet says the vaccines are done.</div>  <div class="callout good">Sleep is training. A tired puppy is a biting puppy, <regex>user_name</regex>.</div></div>	<div class="card">  <h4 class="card-title">New puppy — the first week</h4>  <p class="muted t-small">Buy less than you think. The first week is mostly routine and towels.</p>  <ul class="list">    <li>Same food the breeder was feeding — swap brands slowly over 7 days</li>    <li>Crate or bed in a quiet corner, not the busiest room</li>    <li>Collar + tag, and a lead you can hold with one hand</li>    <li>Two bowls, one for water that stays full</li>    <li>Enzyme cleaner for accidents — normal cleaner leaves the scent mark</li>    <li>Old towels by the door for wet paws</li>    <li>Chew toy and a soft toy. Not your slippers.</li>  </ul>  <div class="divider"></div>  <p class="muted t-small"><strong>First 48 hours</strong></p>  <ol class="list">    <li>Let the pup explore one room. No crowds of visitors.</li>    <li>Vet booked within 3 days for a check + vaccination plan.</li>    <li>Out to toilet every 90 minutes, and after every nap, meal, play.</li>    <li>Praise the second it finishes outside. Ten seconds late and it means nothing to them.</li>  </ol>  <div class="callout warn">No dog parks until the vet says the vaccines are done.</div>  <div class="callout good">Sleep is training. A tired puppy is a biting puppy, .</div></div>	-
26.8.0	checklist/Exam revision week checklist	<div class="card">  <h4 class="card-title">Exam revision week</h4>  <p class="muted t-small">Seven days. Recall beats rereading — test yourself or it doesn't count.</p>  <ul class="list">    <li>Past papers printed, ideally three of them</li>    <li>One page of formulas or key facts, written by hand</li>    <li>Topic list with weak spots starred</li>    <li>Timer — 25 minutes on, 5 off</li>    <li>Phone in another room during blocks</li>    <li>Water bottle on the desk, snacks that aren't crisps</li>    <li>Sleep before midnight. Cramming at 2am costs you marks at 9am.</li>  </ul>  <div class="divider"></div>  <details class="acc">    <summary>The seven-day shape</summary>    <div class="body">      <ul class="list">        <li><strong>Days 1–2:</strong> cover weak topics, make short notes</li>        <li><strong>Days 3–4:</strong> past paper, mark it, list every mistake</li>        <li><strong>Day 5:</strong> fix those mistakes, then a second paper</li>        <li><strong>Day 6:</strong> light review, only your one-pagers</li>        <li><strong>Day 7:</strong> bag packed, route checked, early night</li>      </ul>    </div>  </details>  <div class="callout info">Teaching a topic out loud to an empty room is the fastest way to find the hole, <regex>user_name</regex>.</div></div>	<div class="card">  <h4 class="card-title">Exam revision week</h4>  <p class="muted t-small">Seven days. Recall beats rereading — test yourself or it doesn't count.</p>  <ul class="list">    <li>Past papers printed, ideally three of them</li>    <li>One page of formulas or key facts, written by hand</li>    <li>Topic list with weak spots starred</li>    <li>Timer — 25 minutes on, 5 off</li>    <li>Phone in another room during blocks</li>    <li>Water bottle on the desk, snacks that aren't crisps</li>    <li>Sleep before midnight. Cramming at 2am costs you marks at 9am.</li>  </ul>  <div class="divider"></div