26.12.0	checklist/First apartment utility setup checklist	<div class="card"><h4>First apartment utility setup checklist</h4><ul class="list"><li>Electricity: call provider, give move-in date, ask about deposit</li><li>Gas: confirm if separate provider or bundled with electric</li><li>Water/sewer: often billed via landlord or city; confirm before you panic</li><li>Internet: check available ISPs, book install 2–3 weeks ahead</li><li>Renters insurance: get a quote before move-in (usually cheap)</li><li>Trash pickup: ask landlord if included or if you set up city service</li><li>Update address: bank, subscriptions, driver's license, voter registration</li></ul><p class="t-small muted">Tip: keep confirmation numbers in one note. The internet installer will ask for them.</p></div>	<div class="card"><h4>First apartment utility setup checklist</h4><ul class="list"><li>Electricity: call provider, give move-in date, ask about deposit</li><li>Gas: confirm if separate provider or bundled with electric</li><li>Water/sewer: often billed via landlord or city; confirm before you panic</li><li>Internet: check available ISPs, book install 2–3 weeks ahead</li><li>Renters insurance: get a quote before move-in (usually cheap)</li><li>Trash pickup: ask landlord if included or if you set up city service</li><li>Update address: bank, subscriptions, driver's license, voter registration</li></ul><p class="t-small muted">Tip: keep confirmation numbers in one note. The internet installer will ask for them.</p></div>	-
26.13.0	checklist/Grocery run healthy-ish checklist	<div class="card"><h4>Grocery run healthy-ish checklist</h4><ul class="list"><li>Produce: 2–3 veggies you'll actually cook (broccoli, peppers, spinach)</li><li>Protein: eggs, chicken or tofu, canned beans</li><li>Grains: rice, oats, whole wheat pasta</li><li>Dairy/alt: yogurt or plant milk</li><li>Fruit: apples, bananas, berries</li><li>Snacks: nuts, hummus, popcorn</li><li>Frozen: peas, berries, veggie mix for lazy nights</li><li>Pantry top-up: olive oil, garlic, spices you ran out of</li></ul><p class="t-small muted">Rule of thumb: half the cart fresh, half shelf-stable. You'll eat better and waste less.</p></div>	<div class="card"><h4>Grocery run healthy-ish checklist</h4><ul class="list"><li>Produce: 2–3 veggies you'll actually cook (broccoli, peppers, spinach)</li><li>Protein: eggs, chicken or tofu, canned beans</li><li>Grains: rice, oats, whole wheat pasta</li><li>Dairy/alt: yogurt or plant milk</li><li>Fruit: apples, bananas, berries</li><li>Snacks: nuts, hummus, popcorn</li><li>Frozen: peas, berries, veggie mix for lazy nights</li><li>Pantry top-up: olive oil, garlic, spices you ran out of</li></ul><p class="t-small muted">Rule of thumb: half the cart fresh, half shelf-stable. You'll eat better and waste less.</p></div>	-
26.14.0	checklist/Before a long flight checklist	<div class="card"><h4>Before a long flight checklist</h4><ul class="list"><li>Check passport expiry (6+ months from travel)</li><li>Confirm visa requirements for destination and layovers</li><li>Download offline maps, boarding passes, entertainment</li><li>Pack a small pouch: charger, earbuds, eye mask, toothbrush</li><li>Wear compression socks and loose layers</li><li>Hydrate: buy water after security, skip the free airport wine</li><li>Set phone to airline mode but keep alarms on</li><li>Note local arrival time and how you'll get to lodging</li></ul><p class="t-small muted">Pro tip: set your watch to destination time as soon as you board. Helps with jet lag.</p></div>	<div class="card"><h4>Before a long flight checklist</h4><ul class="list"><li>Check passport expiry (6+ months from travel)</li><li>Confirm visa requirements for destination and layovers</li><li>Download offline maps, boarding passes, entertainment</li><li>Pack a small pouch: charger, earbuds, eye mask, toothbrush</li><li>Wear compression socks and loose layers</li><li>Hydrate: buy water after security, skip the free airport wine</li><li>Set phone to airline mode but keep alarms on</li><li>Note local arrival time and how you'll get to lodging</li></ul><p class="t-small muted">Pro tip: set your watch to destination time as soon as you board. Helps with jet lag.</p></div>	-
26.15.0	checklist/Dinner party prep checklist	<div class="card"><h4>Dinner party prep checklist</h4><ul class="list"><li>Confirm guest count and any allergies/dietary needs</li><li>Plan menu: one main, two sides, one dessert. Keep it simple.</li><li>Shop 1–2 days ahead; chop what you can early</li><li>Clean bathrooms and clear clutter from common areas</li><li>Set table or buffet station with plates, cutlery, napkins</li><li>Chill drinks and prep water pitcher</li><li>Make a playlist (low volume, good background)</li><li>Light candles or dim lights 10 min before arrival</li></ul><p class="t-small muted">Don't aim for perfect. Aim for fed and happy.</p></div>	<div class="card"><h4>Dinner party prep checklist</h4><ul class="list"><li>Confirm guest count and any allergies/dietary needs</li><li>Plan menu: one main, two sides, one dessert. Keep it simple.</li><li>Shop 1–2 days ahead; chop what you can early</li><li>Clean bathrooms and clear clutter from common areas</li><li>Set table or buffet station with plates, cutlery, napkins</li><li>Chill drinks and prep water pitcher</li><li>Make a playlist (low volume, good background)</li><li>Light candles or dim lights 10 min before arrival</li></ul><p class="t-small muted">Don't aim for perfect. Aim for fed and happy.</p></div>	-
26.16.0	checklist/Backyard BBQ checklist	<div class="card"><h4>Backyard BBQ checklist</h4><ul class="list"><li>Clean grill grates and check propane/charcoal supply</li><li>Plan menu: burgers, dogs, one veggie option, sides</li><li>Buy ice, drinks, and cooler</li><li>Prep toppings: lettuce, tomato, onion, pickles, sauces</li><li>Set up shade, seating, and trash/recycling bins</li><li>Bug spray and sunscreen on a side table</li><li>Music and lawn games ready</li><li>Have a rain plan (canopy or move inside)</li></ul><p class="t-small muted">Cook burgers to 160°F. No one wants to remember your BBQ for the wrong reason.</p></div>	<div class="card"><h4>Backyard BBQ checklist</h4><ul class="list"><li>Clean grill grates and check propane/charcoal supply</li><li>Plan menu: burgers, dogs, one veggie option, sides</li><li>Buy ice, drinks, and cooler</li><li>Prep toppings: lettuce, tomato, onion, pickles, sauces</li><li>Set up shade, seating, and trash/recycling bins</li><li>Bug spray and sunscreen on a side table</li><li>Music and lawn games ready</li><li>Have a rain plan (canopy or move inside)</li></ul><p class="t-small muted">Cook burgers to 160°F. No one wants to remember your BBQ for the wrong reason.</p></div>	-
26.17.0	checklist/New job first week checklist	<div class="card"><h4>New job first week checklist</h4><ul class="list"><li>Confirm start time, location, and who to ask for</li><li>Plan outfit and commute route (test it if you can)</li><li>Bring ID, bank details for payroll, and a notebook</li><li>Set up email signature and calendar blocks</li><li>Learn names: write them down, use them</li><li>Ask your manager: what does success look like in 30 days?</li><li>Find the coffee, bathroom, and snack spots</li><li>Schedule a short check-in with your manager for end of week</li></ul><p class="t-small muted">You're not expected to know everything. Asking good questions is the job.</p></div>	<div class="card"><h4>New job first week checklist</h4><ul class="list"><li>Confirm start time, location, and who to ask for</li><li>Plan outfit and commute route (test it if you can)</li><li>Bring ID, bank details for payroll, and a notebook</li><li>Set up email signature and calendar blocks</li><li>Learn names: write them down, use them</li><li>Ask your manager: what does success look like in 30 days?</li><li>Find the coffee, bathroom, and snack spots</li><li>Schedule a short check-in with your manager for end of week</li></ul><p class="t-small muted">You're not expected to know everything. Asking good questions is the job.</p></div>	-
