26.42.0	checklist/Beach day checklist	<div class="umi-page"><div class="card"><h4>Beach day checklist</h4><p class="muted">Sun, sand, and a little planning. Here's what to toss in the bag so you can actually relax.</p><ul class="list"><li><strong>Sunscreen</strong> — SPF 30+, water-resistant. Reapply every 2 hours.</li><li><strong>Towel</strong> — one for sitting, one for drying off. Quick-dry if you have it.</li><li><strong>Water bottle</strong> — freeze it overnight for a cold drink all day.</li><li><strong>Snacks</strong> — fruit, nuts, or a sandwich. Avoid melty chocolate.</li><li><strong>Hat & sunglasses</strong> — shade for your face and eyes.</li><li><strong>Flip-flops or sandals</strong> — for hot sand and rocky bits.</li><li><strong>Book or podcast</strong> — downtime is the point.</li><li><strong>Small cash</strong> — for parking, ice cream, or that beach chair rental.</li><li><strong>Zip bag</strong> — keeps phone and keys sand-free.</li><li><strong>After-sun lotion</strong> — aloe vera feels like a hug.</li></ul><div class="callout info"><p class="t-small">Pro tip: pack a spare plastic bag for wet swimsuits. Your car seats will thank you.</p></div></div></div>	<div class="umi-page"><div class="card"><h4>Beach day checklist</h4><p class="muted">Sun, sand, and a little planning. Here's what to toss in the bag so you can actually relax.</p><ul class="list"><li><strong>Sunscreen</strong> — SPF 30+, water-resistant. Reapply every 2 hours.</li><li><strong>Towel</strong> — one for sitting, one for drying off. Quick-dry if you have it.</li><li><strong>Water bottle</strong> — freeze it overnight for a cold drink all day.</li><li><strong>Snacks</strong> — fruit, nuts, or a sandwich. Avoid melty chocolate.</li><li><strong>Hat & sunglasses</strong> — shade for your face and eyes.</li><li><strong>Flip-flops or sandals</strong> — for hot sand and rocky bits.</li><li><strong>Book or podcast</strong> — downtime is the point.</li><li><strong>Small cash</strong> — for parking, ice cream, or that beach chair rental.</li><li><strong>Zip bag</strong> — keeps phone and keys sand-free.</li><li><strong>After-sun lotion</strong> — aloe vera feels like a hug.</li></ul><div class="callout info"><p class="t-small">Pro tip: pack a spare plastic bag for wet swimsuits. Your car seats will thank you.</p></div></div></div>	-
26.43.0	checklist/Weekly meal prep checklist	<div class="umi-page"><div class="card"><h4>Weekly meal prep checklist</h4><p class="muted">A little Sunday effort saves you from the 6pm "what's for dinner" panic.</p><ul class="list"><li><strong>Plan your menu</strong> — pick 3–4 recipes. Variety is nice, but repetition is easier.</li><li><strong>Check your pantry</strong> — use what you have before buying more.</li><li><strong>Make a grocery list</strong> — organized by aisle. You'll shop faster.</li><li><strong>Shop</strong> — stick to the list, but grab a treat. You're human.</li><li><strong>Wash and chop veggies</strong> — do it all at once. Future you says thanks.</li><li><strong>Cook grains and proteins</strong> — batch-cook rice, quinoa, chicken, or beans.</li><li><strong>Portion into containers</strong> — glass or BPA-free. Label with dates.</li><li><strong>Store smart</strong> — fridge for 3–4 days, freezer for longer.</li><li><strong>Clean as you go</strong> — a tidy kitchen makes the week feel lighter.</li></ul><div class="callout good"><p class="t-small">Start with just two lunches. Momentum beats perfection.</p></div></div></div>	<div class="umi-page"><div class="card"><h4>Weekly meal prep checklist</h4><p class="muted">A little Sunday effort saves you from the 6pm "what's for dinner" panic.</p><ul class="list"><li><strong>Plan your menu</strong> — pick 3–4 recipes. Variety is nice, but repetition is easier.</li><li><strong>Check your pantry</strong> — use what you have before buying more.</li><li><strong>Make a grocery list</strong> — organized by aisle. You'll shop faster.</li><li><strong>Shop</strong> — stick to the list, but grab a treat. You're human.</li><li><strong>Wash and chop veggies</strong> — do it all at once. Future you says thanks.</li><li><strong>Cook grains and proteins</strong> — batch-cook rice, quinoa, chicken, or beans.</li><li><strong>Portion into containers</strong> — glass or BPA-free. Label with dates.</li><li><strong>Store smart</s