26.47.0	checklist/Pet sitter instructions checklist	<div class="umi-page"><div class="card"><h4>Pet sitter instructions checklist</h4><p class="muted">Heading out? Make sure your sitter has everything they need to keep tails wagging.</p><ul class="list"><li><strong>Feeding schedule</strong> — exact amounts, times, and where food is kept.</li><li><strong>Medication</strong> — dosage, timing, and how to administer (with treats if needed).</li><li><strong>Vet contact</strong> — name, number, and address. Also an emergency vet.</li><li><strong>Behavior notes</strong> — shy? escape artist? loves belly rubs? Include it.</li><li><strong>Walk routine</strong> — route, duration, leash habits.</li><li><strong>House rules</strong> — off-limits rooms, furniture, or treats.</li><li><strong>Emergency contact</strong> — you, plus a backup person.</li><li><strong>Supply location</strong> — extra leashes, poop bags, cleaning supplies.</li><li><strong>Wi-Fi password</strong> — for sending you photos, obviously.</li></ul><div class="callout info"><p class="t-small">A quick meet-and-greet before you leave helps everyone feel calmer.</p></div></div></div>	<div class="umi-page"><div class="card"><h4>Pet sitter instructions checklist</h4><p class="muted">Heading out? Make sure your sitter has everything they need to keep tails wagging.</p><ul class="list"><li><strong>Feeding schedule</strong> — exact amounts, times, and where food is kept.</li><li><strong>Medication</strong> — dosage, timing, and how to administer (with treats if needed).</li><li><strong>Vet contact</strong> — name, number, and address. Also an emergency vet.</li><li><strong>Behavior notes</strong> — shy? escape artist? loves belly rubs? Include it.</li><li><strong>Walk routine</strong> — route, duration, leash habits.</li><li><strong>House rules</strong> — off-limits rooms, furniture, or treats.</li><li><strong>Emergency contact</strong> — you, plus a backup person.</li><li><strong>Supply location</strong> — extra leashe