26.48.0	checklist/New mattress first week checklist	<div class="card"><h4>New mattress first week</h4><ul class="list"><li>Leave it to expand for 24 hours before sleeping on it.</li><li>Air it out with windows open to let off that new-foam smell.</li><li>Rotate head-to-foot once, around day three.</li><li>Put on a waterproof protector before any spills happen.</li><li>Give your body a few nights to adjust to the new support.</li><li>Note how it feels each morning. If you wake up sore, use the trial period.</li><li>Wash sheets before first use if they're new too.</li></ul><p class="muted t-small">A mattress adjusts to you, but only if you give it a minute.</p></div>	<div class="card"><h4>New mattress first week</h4><ul class="list"><li>Leave it to expand for 24 hours before sleeping on it.</li><li>Air it out with windows open to let off that new-foam smell.</li><li>Rotate head-to-foot once, around day three.</li><li>Put on a waterproof protector before any spills happen.</li><li>Give your body a few nights to adjust to the new support.</li><li>Note how it feels each morning. If you wake up sore, use the trial period.</li><li>Wash sheets before first use if they're new too.</li></ul><p class="muted t-small">A mattress adjusts to you, but only if you give it a minute.</p></div>	-
26.49.0	checklist/Coffee shop work session checklist	<div class="card"><h4>Coffee shop work session</h4><ul class="list"><li>Charge laptop and phone fully before you leave.</li><li>Pack headphones (over-ear if you get distracted).</li><li>Bring a power strip if you need an outlet and want to make friends.</li><li>Buy something every couple of hours. It's just polite.</li><li>Sit away from the door and the espresso machine if you can.</li><li>Have a backup plan for Wi-Fi flakiness, like a phone hotspot.</li><li>Set a timer so you actually leave when you meant to.</li></ul><p class="muted t-small">A good cafe is a background, not a bedroom. Keep it tidy.</p></div>	<div class="card"><h4>Coffee shop work session</h4><ul class="list"><li>Charge laptop and phone fully before you leave.</li><li>Pack headphones (over-ear if you get distracted).</li><li>Bring a power strip if you need an outlet and want to make friends.</li><li>Buy something every couple of hours. It's just polite.</li><li>Sit away from the door and the espresso machine if you can.</li><li>Have a backup plan for Wi-Fi flakiness, like a phone hotspot.</li><li>Set a timer so you actually leave when you meant to.</li></ul><p class="muted t-small">A good cafe is a background, not a bedroom. Keep it tidy.</p></div>	-
26.50.0	checklist/First day at a new gym checklist	<div class="card"><h4>First day at a new gym</h4><ul class="list"><li>Bring a lock if lockers aren't digital, and a water bottle.</li><li>Wear clothes you can move in. No need for matching sets.</li><li>Do the tour or orientation if they offer one. It's not a trap.</li><li>Start with 20 minutes on something easy. You're just showing up.</li><li>Wipe down machines after use. The spray bottles are your friend.</li><li>Ask staff where things live if you can't find them. That's what they're for.</li><li>Leave before you're exhausted. You want to come back tomorrow.</li></ul><p class="muted t-small">Nobody is watching you. They're all busy checking their own form.</p></div>	<div class="card"><h4>First day at a new gym</h4><ul class="list"><li>Bring a lock if lockers aren't digital, and a water bottle.</li><li>Wear clothes you can move in. No need for matching sets.</li><li>Do the tour or orientation if they offer one. It's not a trap.</li><li>Start with 20 minutes on something easy. You're just showing up.</li><li>Wipe down machines after use. The spray bottles are your friend.</li><li>Ask staff where things live if you can't find them. That's what they're for.</li><li>Leave before you're exhausted. You want to come back tomorrow.</li></ul><p class="muted t-small">Nobody is watching you. They're all busy checking their own form.</p></div>	-
26.51.0	checklist/Making a budget spreadsheet checklist	<div class="card"><h4>Making a budget spreadsheet</h4><ul class="list"><li>List all income sources for a typical month.</li><li>List fixed expenses: rent, utilities, subscriptions, loan payments.</li><li>Estimate variable expenses: groceries, gas, fun money.</li><li>Subtract expenses from income. If negative, trim the fun first.</li><li>Add a column for actual spending to compare later.</li><li>Color-code or bold the categories that matter most to you.</li><li>Set a date to review it, like the first Sunday of each month.</li></ul><p class="muted t-small">A budget is just a plan you can edit. No shame in revisions.</p></div>	<div class="card"><h4>Making a budget spreadsheet</h4><ul class="list"><li>List all income sources for a typical month.</li><li>List fixed expenses: rent, utilities, subscriptions, loan payments.</li><li>Estimate variable expenses: groceries, gas, fun money.</li><li>Subtract expenses from income. If negative, trim the fun first.</li><li>Add a column for actual spending to compare later.</li><li>Color-code or bold the categories that matter most to you.</li><li>Set a date to review it, like the first Sunday of each month.</li></ul><p class="muted t-small">A budget is just a plan you can edit. No shame in revisions.</p></div>	-
26.52.0	checklist/Monthly car maintenance checklist	<div class="card"><h4>Monthly car maintenance</h4><ul class="list"><li>Check tire pressure, including the spare.</li><li>Top off windshield washer fluid if low.</li><li>Look at oil level with the engine cool.</li><li>Test all lights: headlights, brake lights, turn signals.</li><li>Check wiper blades for cracks or streaks.</li><li>Clear out trash and anything rolling around.</li><li>Note any new noises or dashboard lights for your mechanic.</li></ul><p class="muted t-small">Five minutes a month saves a lot of roadside waiting.</p></div>	<div class="card"><h4>Monthly car maintenance</h4><ul class="list"><li>Check tire pressure, including the spare.</li><li>Top off windshield washer fluid if low.</li><li>Look at oil level with the engine cool.</li><li>Test all lights: headlights, brake lights, turn signals.</li><li>Check wiper blades for cracks or streaks.</li><li>Clear out trash and anything rolling around.</li><li>Note any new noises or dashboard lights for your mechanic.</li></ul><p class="muted t-small">Five minutes a month saves a lot of roadside waiting.</p></div>	-
26.53.0	checklist/Before a phone repair appointment checklist	<div class="card"><h4>Before a phone repair</h4><ul class="list"><li>Back up photos, contacts, and messages to the cloud or a computer.</li><li>Note your passcode and Apple ID or Google password somewhere safe.</li><li>Sign out of banking and payment apps if you can.</li><li>Remove the SIM card and any case or screen protector.</li><li>Write down the exact problem, including when it started.</li><li>Bring your charger and cable to test after the fix.</li><li>Ask for a time estimate and warranty details before you leave.</li></ul><p class="muted t-small">A backup is the only thing standing between you and a very quiet week.</p></div>	<div class="card"><h4>Before a phone repair</h4><ul class="list"><li>Back up photos, contacts, and messages to the cloud or a computer.</li><li>Note your passcode and Apple ID or Google password somewhere safe.</li><li>Sign out of banking and payment apps if you can.</li><li>Remove the SIM card and any case or screen protector.</li><li>Write down the exact problem, including when it started.</li><li>Bring your charger and cable to test after the fix.</li><li>Ask for a time estimate and warranty details before you leave.</li></ul><p class="muted t-small">A backup is the only thing standing between you and a very quiet week.</p></div>	-
