26.58.0	checklist/Rainy day at-home checklist	<div class="card"><h4>Rainy day at home</h4><p class="muted t-small">Cancel plans, embrace puddles. Here's your menu.</p><ul class="list"><li>Make a warm drink, take your time</li><li>Put on socks and something soft</li><li>Start a puzzle, book, or easy game</li><li>Bake something simple if you feel like it</li><li>Call a friend you owe a chat</li><li>Do one small home reset: blanket, dishes, candle</li><li>Watch the rain for five minutes doing nothing else</li></ul></div>	<div class="card"><h4>Rainy day at home</h4><p class="muted t-small">Cancel plans, embrace puddles. Here's your menu.</p><ul class="list"><li>Make a warm drink, take your time</li><li>Put on socks and something soft</li><li>Start a puzzle, book, or easy game</li><li>Bake something simple if you feel like it</li><li>Call a friend you owe a chat</li><li>Do one small home reset: blanket, dishes, candle</li><li>Watch the rain for five minutes doing nothing else</li></ul></div>	-
26.59.0	checklist/Gym bag packing checklist	<div class="card"><h4>Gym bag packing</h4><p class="muted t-small">Lace up, <regex>user_name</regex>. No midnight locker runs.</p><ul class="list"><li>Gym clothes: top, bottoms, socks</li><li>Trainers or specialised shoes</li><li>Water bottle, filled</li><li>Towel, small one for face</li><li>Toiletries: deodorant, hair tie, flip-flops if showering</li><li>Padlock for the locker</li><li>Headphones, charged</li><li>Post-workout snack if you'll be hungry</li></ul></div>	<div class="card"><h4>Gym bag packing</h4><p class="muted t-small">Lace up, . No midnight locker runs.</p><ul class="list"><li>Gym clothes: top, bottoms, socks</li><li>Trainers or specialised shoes</li><li>Water bottle, filled</li><li>Towel, small one for face</li><li>Toiletries: deodorant, hair tie, flip-flops if showering</li><li>Padlock for the locker</li><li>Headphones, charged</li><li>Post-workout snack if you'll be hungry</li></ul></div>	-
26.60.0	checklist/Sick day recovery checklist	<div class="card"><h4>Sick day recovery checklist</h4><p class="muted">Rest is the main event. Everything else is supporting cast.</p><ul class="list"><li>Take your temperature and note it</li><li>Set a water bottle within arm's reach</li><li>Take any meds on schedule</li><li>Queue up something low-effort to watch</li><li>Text one person so they know you're down</li><li>Cancel or reschedule today's obligations</li><li>Nap without guilt</li><li>Eat something bland if you can</li><li>Check in with yourself after 4 hours</li><li>Plan a slow re-entry tomorrow</li></ul><details class="acc"><summary>Emergency signs🚨</summary><div class="body"><p>Difficulty breathing, chest pain, confusion, or a fever that won't budge — get medical help, don't wait.</p></div></details></div>	<div class="card"><h4>Sick day recovery checklist</h4><p class="muted">Rest is the main event. Everything else is supporting cast.</p><ul class="list"><li>Take your temperature and note it</li><li>Set a water bottle within arm's reach</li><li>Take any meds on schedule</li><li>Queue up something low-effort to watch</li><li>Text one person so they know you're down</li><li>Cancel or reschedule today's obligations</li><li>Nap without guilt</li><li>Eat something bland if you can</li><li>Check in with yourself after 4 hours</li><li>Plan a slow re-entry tomorrow</li></ul><details class="acc"><summary>Emergency signs🚨</summary><div class="body"><p>Difficulty breathing, chest pain, confusion, or a fever that won't budge — get medical help, don't wait.</p></div></details></div>	-
26.61.0	checklist/Public speaking practice checklist	<div class="card"><h4>Public speaking practice checklist</h4><p class="muted">Confidence is built in the run-through, not the moment.</p><ul class="list"><li>Write your opening line word-for-word</li><li>Outline three main beats</li><li>Record yourself once and watch it back</li><li>Time the whole thing</li><li>Mark spots to pause or breathe</li><li>Practice out loud standing up</li><li>Trim any slide that needs explaining</li><li>Rehearse the closing line until it's automatic</li><li>Do a final run in the actual room if possible</li><li>Pick one friendly face to start with</li></ul><details class="acc"><summary>If you freeze🧊</summary><div class="body"><p>Pause. Take a breath. Say “Let me put that another way.” Then repeat your last point. The audience won't mind.</p></div></details></div>	<div class="card"><h4>Public speaking practice checklist</h4><p class="muted">Confidence is built in the run-through, not the moment.</p><ul class="list"><li>Write your opening line word-for-word</li><li>Outline three main beats</li><li>Record yourself once and watch it back</li><li>Time the whole thing</li><li>Mark spots to pause or breathe</li><li>Practice out loud standing up</li><li>Trim any slide that needs explaining</li><li>Rehearse the closing line until it's automatic</li><li>Do a final run in the actual room if possible</li><li>Pick one friendly face to start with</li></ul><details class="acc"><summary>If you freeze🧊</summary><div class="body"><p>Pause. Take a breath. Say “Let me put that another way.” Then repeat your last point. The audience won't mind.</p></div></details></div>	-
26.62.0	checklist/Morning stretch routine checklist	<div class="card"><h4>Morning stretch routine checklist</h4><p class="muted">Five minutes now saves your neck from a long day later.</p><ul class="list"><li>Stand and reach tall for 10 seconds</li><li>Neck rolls: slow, both directions</li><li>Shoulder shrugs — up, back, down</li><li>Side bend left, hold, then right</li><li>Gentle forward fold, knees soft</li><li>Cat-cow on all fours, 5 rounds</li><li>Seated spinal twist each side</li><li>Hip flexor stretch, 30 sec per leg</li><li>Ankle circles, both feet</li><li>Deep breath in, big sigh out — done</li></ul><details class="acc"><summary>Make it stick📌</summary><div class="body"><p>Pair it with something you already do — after brushing teeth, before coffee. Same trigger, same routine.</p></div></details></div>	<div class="card"><h4>Morning stretch routine checklist</h4><p class="muted">Five minutes now saves your neck from a long day later.</p><ul class="list"><li>Stand and reach tall for 10 seconds</li><li>Neck rolls: slow, both directions</li><li>Shoulder shrugs — up, back, down</li><li>Side bend left, hold, then right</li><li>Gentle forward fold, knees soft</li><li>Cat-cow on all fours, 5 rounds</li><li>Seated spinal twist each side</li><li>Hip flexor stretch, 30 sec per leg</li><li>Ankle circles, both feet</li><li>Deep breath in, big sigh out — done</li></ul><details class="acc"><summary>Make it stick📌</summary><div class="body"><p>Pair it with something you already do — after brushing teeth, before coffee. Same trigger, same routine.</p></div></details></div>	-
26.63.0	checklist/Email inbox zero checklist	<div class="card"><h4>Email inbox zero checklist</h4><p class="muted">You're not filing; you're deciding. Every message gets a verb.</p><ul class="list"><li>Sort by sender to batch similar emails</li><li>Delete or archive anything you'll never need</li><li>Unsubscribe from three lists you ignore</li><li>Reply if it takes under two minutes</li><li>Turn longer replies into a task with a due date</li><li>Forward anything that belongs to someone else</li><li>Star the ones waiting on a reply from others</li><li>Empty your trash and spam folders</li><li>Repeat until inbox shows zero unread</li><li>Set a time tomorrow for the next pass</li></ul><details class="acc"><summary>If it feels endless🌀</summary><div class="body"><p>Do it in 15-minute sprints. Progress beats perfection. A smaller inbox tomorrow is still a win.</p></div></details></div>	<div class="card"><h4>Email inbox zero checklist</h4><p class="muted">You're not filing; you're deciding. Every message gets a verb.</p><ul class="list"><li>Sort by sender to batch similar emails</li><li>Delete or archive anything you'll never need</li><li>Unsubscribe from three lists you ignore</li><li>Reply if it takes under two minutes</li><li>Turn longer replies into a task with a due date</li><li>Forward anything that belongs to someone else</li><li>Star the ones waiting on a reply from others</li><li>Empty your trash and spam folders</li><li>Repeat until inbox shows zero unread</li><li>Set a time tomorrow for the next pass</li></ul><details class="acc"><summary>If it feels endless🌀</summary><div class="body"><p>Do it in 15-minute sprints. Progress beats perfection. A smaller inbox tomorrow is still a win.</p></div></details></div>	-
26.0.1	checklist/Digital declutter checklist	<div class="card"><h4>Digital declutter checklist</h4><p class="muted">Less digital noise, more brain space.</p><ul class="list"><li>Delete apps you haven't opened in a month</li><li>Unsubscribe from five email lists</li><li>Clear your downloads folder</li><li>Organize photos into year folders</li><li>Back up important files to cloud or drive</li><li>Empty your desktop into a single folder</li><li>Turn off non-essential notifications</li><li>Unfollow three accounts that drain you</li><li>Clear browser bookmarks bar of dead links</li><li>Set a weekly 10-minute tidy reminder</li></ul><details class="acc"><summary>Start with one device📱</summary><div class="body"><p>Pick your phone first — it's where the clutter hurts most. Then move to laptop if you have energy left.</p></div></details></div>	<div class="card"><h4>Digital declutter checklist</h4><p class="muted">Less digital noise, more brain space.</p><ul class="list"><li>Delete apps you haven't opened in a month</li><li>Unsubscribe from five email lists</li><li>Clear your downloads folder</li><li>Organize photos into year folders</li><li>Back up important files to cloud or drive</li><li>Empty your desktop into a single folder</li><li>Turn off non-essential notifications</li><li>Unfollow three accounts that drain you</li><li>Clear browser bookmarks bar of dead links</li><li>Set a weekly 10-minute tidy reminder</li></ul><details class="acc"><summary>Start with one device📱</summary><div class="body"><p>Pick your phone first — it's where the clutter hurts most. Then move to laptop if you have energy left.</p></div></details></div>	-
26.1.1	checklist/Decluttering one room checklist	<div class="card"><h4>Decluttering one room checklist</h4><p class="muted">One room, one afternoon. You've got this.</p><ul class="list"><li>Pick a single room and set a timer for 30 minutes</li><li>Grab three bags: keep, donate, toss</li><li>Clear one surface completely first</li><li>Work top to bottom, left to right</li><li>Ask “used in the last year?” for each item</li><li>Put donate bag in your car immediately</li><li>Wipe down surfaces you uncover</li><li>Find a home for everything you keep</li><li>Take out trash and recycling</li><li>Notice the space and breathe</li></ul><details class="acc"><summary>If you get stuck🤔</summary><div class="body"><p>Start with trash. It's the easiest decision and it builds momentum.</p></div></details></div>	<div class="card"><h4>Decluttering one room checklist</h4><p class="muted">One room, one afternoon. You've got this.</p><ul class="list"><li>Pick a single room and set a timer for 30 minutes</li><li>Grab three bags: keep, donate, toss</li><li>Clear one surface completely first</li><li>Work top to bottom, left to right</li><li>Ask “used in the last year?” for each item</li><li>Put donate bag in your car immediately</li><li>Wipe down surfaces you uncover</li><li>Find a home for everything you keep</li><li>Take out trash and recycling</li><li>Notice the space and breathe</li></ul><details class="acc"><summary>If you get stuck🤔</summary><div class="body"><p>Start with trash. It's the easiest decision and it builds momentum.</p></div></details></div>	-
