26.5.1	checklist/Starting a small compost bin checklist	<div class="card">  <h4>Starting a small compost bin checklist</h4>  <p class="muted t-small">Greens smell, browns save you. Balance is the whole game.</p>  <ul class="list">    <li>Pick a spot: shade, drainage, reachable in the rain</li>    <li>Get a lidded bin or a sturdy corner pile</li>    <li>Keep a small caddy in the kitchen with a liner</li>    <li>Add greens: veg scraps, coffee grounds, grass clippings</li>    <li>Add browns: cardboard, dry leaves, egg cartons, paper</li>    <li>Aim for roughly two parts brown to one part green</li>    <li>Turn or poke it weekly so it can breathe</li>    <li>Keep out: meat, dairy, oils, pet waste, treated wood</li>  </ul>  <div class="callout info">    <p>If it smells sour, add browns and turn it. If it's bone dry, add a splash of water. That's the whole troubleshooting guide.</p>  </div>  <p class="muted t-small">Good luck, <regex>user_name</regex>. First bucket of finished compost feels like finding money in a coat pocket.</p></div>	<div class="card">  <h4>Starting a small compost bin checklist</h4>  <p class="muted t-small">Greens smell, browns save you. Balance is the whole game.</p>  <ul class="list">    <li>Pick a spot: shade, drainage, reachable in the rain</li>    <li>Get a lidded bin or a sturdy corner pile</li>    <li>Keep a small caddy in the kitchen with a liner</li>    <li>Add greens: veg scraps, coffee grounds, grass clippings</li>    <li>Add browns: cardboard, dry leaves, egg cartons, paper</li>    <li>Aim for roughly two parts brown to one part green</li>    <li>Turn or poke it weekly so it can breathe</li>    <li>Keep out: meat, dairy, oils, pet waste, treated wood</li>  </ul>  <div class="callout info">    <p>If it smells sour, add browns and turn it. If it's bone dry, add a splash of water. That's the whole troubleshooting guide.</p>  </div>  <p class="muted t-small">Good luck, . First bucket of finished compost feels 