31.43.0	colour_palette/Colours of a classic dartboard (standard clock)	<div class="card"><h4>Dartboard, standard 20-sector clock</h4><p class="t-small muted">Same two colours doubled up: dark sectors, light sectors, and the two rings that pay better. Here's the working set, <regex>user_name</regex>.</p><div class="grid two"><div class="stat"><span class="label">Black</span><span class="value" style="color:#1c1a17">#1C1A17</span></div><div class="stat"><span class="label">Cream</span><span class="value" style="color:#e9dfc6">#E9DFC6</span></div><div class="stat"><span class="label">Treble red</span><span class="value" style="color:#b21e28">#B21E28</span></div><div class="stat"><span class="label">Double green</span><span class="value" style="color:#1d6b3a">#1D6B3A</span></div><div class="stat"><span class="label">Wire</span><span class="value" style="color:#b9b3a6">#B9B3A6</span></div><div class="stat"><span class="label">Number ring</span><span class="value" style="color:#f2f0ea">#F2F0EA</span></div></div><details class="acc"><summary>Which colour is the 20?</summary><div class="body"><p class="t-small">The 20 sits at the top and is black. Sectors alternate black and cream all the way round, so odd numbers land on black and evens on cream in the standard numbering.</p></div></details></div>	<div class="card"><h4>Dartboard, standard 20-sector clock</h4><p class="t-small muted">Same two colours doubled up: dark sectors, light sectors, and the two rings that pay better. Here's the working set, .</p><div class="grid two"><div class="stat"><span class="label">Black</span><span class="value" style="color:#1c1a17">#1C1A17</span></div><div class="stat"><span class="label">Cream</span><span class="value" style="color:#e9dfc6">#E9DFC6</span></div><div class="stat"><span class="label">Treble red</span><span class="value" style="color:#b21e28">#B21E28</span></div><div class="stat"><span class="label">Double green</span><span class="value" style="color:#1d6b3a">#1D6B3A</span></div><div class="stat"><span class="label">Wire</span><span class="value" style="color:#b9b3a6">#B9B3A6</span></div><div class="stat"><span class="label">Number ring</span><span class="value" style="color:#f2f0ea">#F2F0EA</span></div></div><details class="acc"><summary>Which colour is the 20?</summary><div class="body"><p class="t-small">The 20 sits at the top and is black. Sectors alternate black and cream all the way round, so odd numbers land on black and evens on cream in the standard numbering.</p></div></details></div>	-
31.44.0	colour_palette/Colours of a classic traffic cone	<div class="card"><h4>Traffic cones</h4><p class="t-small muted">Sleeve colour is the whole message, <regex>user_name</regex>. Here's what each one is telling you on a UK road.</p><div class="grid two"><div class="stat"><span class="label">Orange sleeve</span><span class="value" style="color:#e2611b">#E2611B</span></div><div class="stat"><span class="label">Reflective band</span><span class="value" style="color:#f5f2e8">#F5F2E8</span></div><div class="stat"><span class="label">Base rubber</span><span class="value" style="color:#232120">#232120</span></div><div class="stat"><span class="label">Blue sleeve</span><span class="value" style="color:#1b4f9c">#1B4F9C</span></div><div class="stat"><span class="label">Green sleeve</span><span class="value" style="color:#1f7a45">#1F7A45</span></div><div class="stat"><span class="label">Red and white</span><span class="value" style="color:#c0242a">#C0242A</span></div></div><details class="acc"><summary>What do blue and green mean?</summary><div class="body"><p class="t-small">Blue marks a works site entrance or a lane closed for a vehicle crossover. Green flags a temporary access point on a footway. Red-and-white cones mark school zones and pedestrian crossings.</p></div></details></div>	<div class="card"><h4>Traffic cones</h4><p class="t-small muted">Sleeve colour is the whole message, . Here's what each one is telling you on a UK road.</p><div class="grid two"><div class="stat"><span class="label">Orange sleeve</span><span class="value" style="color:#e2611b">#E2611B</span></div><div class="stat"><span class="label">Reflective band</span><span class="value" style="color:#f5f2e8">#F5F2E8</span></div><div class="stat"><span class="label">Base rubber</span><span class="value" style="color:#232120">#232120</span></div><div class="stat"><span class="label">Blue sleeve</span><span class="value" style="color:#1b4f9c">#1B4F9C</span></div><div class="stat"><span class