31.45.0	colour_palette/Colours of a classic arcade cabinet marquee (80s set)	<div class="card"><h4>Arcade marquee, early eighties</h4><p class="t-small muted">A backlit plastic strip did a lot of shouting. These are the shades that showed up again and again, <regex>user_name</regex>.</p><div class="grid two"><div class="stat"><span class="label">Hot magenta</span><span class="value" style="color:#e5177f">#E5177F</span></div><div class="stat"><span class="label">Cabinet red</span><span class="value" style="color:#d3222a">#D3222A</span></div><div class="stat"><span class="label">Bird yellow</span><span class="value" style="color:#f5c518">#F5C518</span></div><div class="stat"><span class="label">CRT cyan</span><span class="value" style="color:#28c2d1">#28C2D1</span></div><div class="stat"><span class="label">Deep navy</span><span class="value" style="color:#1b2050">#1B2050</span></div><div class="stat"><span class="label">Black bezel</span><span class="value" style="color:#131314">#131314</span></div></div><details class="acc"><summary>Why so few greens?</summary><div class="body"><p class="t-small">Green dyes on backlit acetate went muddy under a warm bulb, so designers leaned on magenta, cyan and yellow instead. Greenery mostly stayed on the screen side.</p></div></details></div>	<div class="card"><h4>Arcade marquee, early eighties</h4><p class="t-small muted">A backlit plastic strip did a lot of shouting. These are the shades that showed up again and again, .</p><div class="grid two"><div class="stat"><span class="label">Hot magenta</span><span class="value" style="color:#e5177f">#E5177F</span></div><div class="stat"><span class="label">Cabinet red</span><span class="value" style="color:#d3222a">#D3222A</span></div><div class="stat"><span class="label">Bird yellow</span><span class="value" style="color:#f5c518">#F5C518</span></div><div class="stat"><span class="label">CRT cyan</span><span class="value" style="color:#28c2d1">#28C2D1</span></div><div class