31.46.0	colour_palette/Colours of a classic pinball table (Playfield set)	<div class="card"><h4>Pinball playfield, classic set</h4><p class="t-small muted">Saturated, silkscreened, and never shy. Six that carry a whole table, <regex>user_name</regex>.</p><div class="grid two"><div class="stat"><span class="label">Playfield red</span><span class="value" style="color:#d8221f">#D8221F</span></div><div class="stat"><span class="label">Bumper yellow</span><span class="value" style="color:#f2b705">#F2B705</span></div><div class="stat"><span class="label">Ramp blue</span><span class="value" style="color:#1553b8">#1553B8</span></div><div class="stat"><span class="label">Skill-shot green</span><span class="value" style="color:#1a8a53">#1A8A53</span></div><div class="stat"><span class="label">Purple lane</span><span class="value" style="color:#5a2b8c">#5A2B8C</span></div><div class="stat"><span class="label">Gloss black</span><span class="value" style="color:#121214">#121214</span></div></div><details class="acc"><summary>Where does the colour actually go?</summary><div class="body"><p class="t-small">Red and yellow take the high-scoring hits so the eye lands there. Blue and green pick out ramps and lanes to aim at. Purple usually marks a bonus or a multiball path.</p></div></details></div>	<div class="card"><h4>Pinball playfield, classic set</h4><p class="t-small muted">Saturated, silkscreened, and never shy. Six that carry a whole table, .</p><div class="grid two"><div class="stat"><span class="label">Playfield red</span><span class="value" style="color:#d8221f">#D8221F</span></div><div class="stat"><span class="label">Bumper yellow</span><span class="value" style="color:#f2b705">#F2B705</span></div><div class="stat"><span class="label">Ramp blue</span><span class="value" style="color:#1553b8">#1553B8</span></div><div class="stat"><span class="label">Skill-shot green</span><span class="value" style="color:#1a8a53">#1A8A53</span></div><div class="stat"><span clas