34.42.0	http_status_table/HTTP Codes When Wi-Fi Hates You	<div class="stack"><p class="muted">When the signal flickers, the code tells the story.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Code</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>200</td><td>Page loaded, Wi-Fi behaving</td></tr><tr><td>301</td><td>Router redirected you to the login page</td></tr><tr><td>403</td><td>Captive portal says no</td></tr><tr><td>408</td><td>Request timed out waiting for signal</td></tr><tr><td>429</td><td>Too many devices on this network</td></tr><tr><td>502</td><td>Router got a bad response from the modem</td></tr><tr><td>503</td><td>Network temporarily unavailable</td></tr><tr><td>504</td><td>Modem never replied</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class="t-small dim">Tip: 502/504 often mean the router is fine but the modem is napping.</p></div>	<div class="stack"><p class="muted">When the signal flickers, the code tells the story.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Code</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>200</td><td>Page loaded, Wi-Fi behaving</td></tr><tr><td>301</td><td>Router redirected you to the login page</td></tr><tr><td>403</td><td>Captive portal says no</td></tr><tr><td>408</td><td>Request timed out waiting for signal</td></tr><tr><td>429</td><td>Too many devices on this network</td></tr><tr><td>502</td><td>Router got a bad response from the modem</td></tr><tr><td>503</td><td>Network temporarily unavailable</td></tr><tr><td>504</td><td>Modem never replied</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class="t-small dim">Tip: 502/504 often mean the router is fine but the modem is napping.</p></div>	-
