34.54.0	http_status_table/HTTP Codes for Cloud Storage Sync	<div class="stack"><p class="t-small muted">When your files ghost the cloud, <regex>user_name</regex>, these are the numbers in the logs.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Code</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>200</td><td>OK — file synced cleanly</td></tr><tr><td>201</td><td>Created — new folder or file uploaded</td></tr><tr><td>204</td><td>No Content — delete succeeded, nothing to return</td></tr><tr><td>304</td><td>Not Modified — unchanged, skip the transfer</td></tr><tr><td>401</td><td>Unauthorized — token expired, re-login</td></tr><tr><td>403</td><td>Forbidden — shared folder permissions</td></tr><tr><td>409</td><td>Conflict — two devices edited same file</td></tr><tr><td>413</td><td>Payload Too Large — file over quota</td></tr><tr><td>423</td><td>Locked — file checked out elsewhere</td></tr><tr><td>507</td><td>Insufficient Storage — cloud is full</td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class="acc"><summary>Why 409 is the scary one</summary><div class="body"><p class="t-small">It means two truths exist at once. Your client has to pick a winner or merge. Check the conflict copy.</p></div></details></div>	<div class="stack"><p class="t-small muted">When your files ghost the cloud, , these are the numbers in the logs.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Code</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>200</td><td>OK — file synced cleanly</td></tr><tr><td>201</td><td>Created — new folder or file uploaded</td></tr><tr><td>204</td><td>No Content — delete succeeded, nothing to return</td></tr><tr><td>304</td><td>Not Modified — unchanged, skip the transfer</td></tr><tr><td>401</td><td>Unauthorized — token expired, re-login</td></tr><tr><td>403</td><td>Forbidden — shared folder permissions</td></tr><tr><td>409</td><td>Conflict — two devices edited same file</td></tr><tr><td>413</td><td>Payload Too Large — file over quota</td></tr><tr><td>423</td><td>Locked — file checked out elsewhere</td></tr><tr><td>507</td><td>Insufficient Storage — cloud is full</td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class="acc"><summary>Why 409 is the scary one</summary><div class="body"><p class="t-small">It means two truths exist at once. Your client has to pick a winner or merge. Check the conflict copy.</p></div></details></div>	-
34.55.0	http_status_table/HTTP Codes for Podcast Downloads	<div class="stack"><p class="t-small muted">Podcast queue stuck, <regex>user_name</regex>? The feed is speaking HTTP at you.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Code</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>200</td><td>OK — feed or MP3 delivered</td></tr><tr><td>206</td><td>Partial Content — resumed download after pause</td></tr><tr><td>301</td><td>Moved Permanently — feed URL changed, update it</td></tr><tr><td>304</td><td>Not Modified — no new episodes, cache is fine</td></tr><tr><td>404</td><td>Not Found — episode pulled or feed moved</td></tr><tr><td>410</td><td>Gone — show ended, feed retired</td></tr><tr><td>416</td><td>Range Not Satisfiable — bad seek offset</td></tr><tr><td>429</td><td>Too Many Requests — CDN throttling binge downloads</td></tr><tr><td>503</td><td>Service Unavailable — host overloaded at drop time</td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class="acc"><summary>206 in plain words</summary><div class="body"><p class="t-small">It's the thumbs-up for "finish what you started." Your app asked for bytes 400000–800000 and got exactly that.</p></div></details></div>	<div class="stack"><p class="t-small muted">Podcast queue stuck, ? The feed is speaking HTTP at you.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Code</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>200</td><td>OK — feed or MP3 delivered</td></tr><tr><td>206</td><td>Partial Content — resumed download after pause</td></tr><tr><td>301</td><td>Moved Permanently — feed URL changed, update it</td></tr><tr><td>304</td><td>Not Modified — no new episodes, cache is fine</td></tr><tr><td>404</td><td>Not Found — episode pulled or feed moved</td></tr><tr><td>410</td><td>Gone — show ended, feed retired</td></tr><tr><td>416</td><td>Range Not Satisfiable — bad seek offset</td></tr><tr><td>429</td><td>Too Many Requests — CDN throttling binge downloads</td></tr><tr><td>503</td><td>Service Unavailable — host overloaded at drop time</td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class="acc"><summary>206 in plain words</summary><div class="body"><p class="t-small">It's the thumbs-up for "finish what you started." Your app asked for bytes 400000–800000 and got exactly that.</p></div></details></div>	-
34.56.0	http_status_table/HTTP Codes for Hotel Booking APIs	<div class="stack"><p class="t-small muted">Booking a room, <regex>user_name</regex>? Here's what the hotel's backend tries to tell the front desk.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Code</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>200</td><td>OK — availability returned</td></tr><tr><td>201</td><td>Created — reservation confirmed</td></tr><tr><td>200</td><td>No Content — cancellation succeeded</td></tr><tr><td>400</td><td>Bad Request — dates backwards or missing guest</td></tr><tr><td>401</td><td>Unauthorized — loyalty token expired</td></tr><tr><td>409</td><td>Conflict — room taken between quote and book</td></tr><tr><td>422</td><td>Unprocessable — past check-in date</td></tr><tr><td>429</td><td>Too Many Requests — rate limit on search endpoint</td></tr><tr><td>503</td><td>Service Unavailable — PMS down during peak</td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class="acc"><summary>409 is the cruel one</summary><div class="body"><p class="t-small">The room existed when you looked, vanished when you clicked. Re-check availability before charging.</p></div></details></div>	<div class="stack"><p class="t-small muted">Booking a room, ? Here's what the hotel's backend tries to tell the front desk.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Code</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>200</td><td>OK — availability returned</td></tr><tr><td>201</td><td>Created — reservation confirmed</td></tr><tr><td>200</td><td>No Content — cancellation succeeded</td></tr><tr><td>400</td><td>Bad Request — dates backwards or missing guest</td></tr><tr><td>401</td><td>Unauthorized — loyalty token expired</td></tr><tr><td>409</td><td>Conflict — room taken between quote and book</td></tr><tr><td>422</td><td>Unprocessable — past check-in date</td></tr><tr><td>429</td><td>Too Many Requests — rate limit on search endpoint</td></tr><tr><td>503</td><td>Service Unavailable — PMS down during peak</td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class="acc"><summary>409 is the cruel one</summary><div class="body"><p class="t-small">The room existed when you looked, vanished when you clicked. Re-check availability before charging.</p></div></details></div>	-
