34.14.1	http_status_table/HTTP Codes for Hiking Trails	<div class="card"><div class="card-title">HTTP Codes for Hiking Trails</div><p class="muted">Hey <regex>user_name</regex> — every trail is a request. Here's what the mountain replies with.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Code</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>200 OK</td><td>You reached the summit. Trail delivered exactly what it promised.</td></tr><tr><td>301 Moved Permanently</td><td>The old path is closed for regrowth. Take the reroute, it's better anyway.</td></tr><tr><td>304 Not Modified</td><td>Same view as last time, clouds didn't move. Still worth it.</td></tr><tr><td>400 Bad Request</td><td>You started at noon in flip-flops. The trail is confused.</td></tr><tr><td>401 Unauthorized</td><td>Posted. You need a permit, friend.</td></tr><tr><td>403 Forbidden</td><td>Private land. The cows have right of way, not you.</td></tr><tr><td>404 Not Found</td><td>The trailhead sign said "easy loop." It lied. Or you missed the turn.</td></tr><tr><td>408 Request Timeout</td><td>You stopped for a snack. The daylight left without you.</td></tr><tr><td>413 Payload Too Large</td><td>That pack. Ten liters of water and a cast-iron pan?</td></tr><tr><td>429 Too Many Requests</td><td>Popular trail on a Saturday. Everyone gets throttled.</td></tr><tr><td>500 Internal Server Error</td><td>You forgot matches, map, and common sense. The trail can't help with that.</td></tr><tr><td>502 Bad Gateway</td><td>Bridge is out. The far side is unreachable from here.</td></tr><tr><td>503 Service Unavailable</td><td>Trail closed for mud season. Come back in May.</td></tr><tr><td>504 Gateway Timeout</td><td>You waited for the summit view. The fog never cleared.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>	<div class="card"><div class="card-title">HTTP Codes for Hiking Trails</div><p class="muted">Hey  — every trail is a request. Here's what the mountain replies with.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Code