34.16.1	http_status_table/HTTP Codes for Public Transit	<div class="card"><div class="card-title">HTTP Codes for Public Transit</div><p class="muted">Here you go, <regex>user_name</regex>. The bus is a server. You are a polite little request packet.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Code</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>100 Continue</td><td>Bus is approaching. Keep standing at the curb. Keep hoping.</td></tr><tr><td>200 OK</td><td>You boarded. You found a seat. The driver smiled. A miracle.</td></tr><tr><td>301 Moved Permanently</td><td>Stop relocated due to construction. Forever. Get used to it.</td></tr><tr><td>304 Not Modified</td><td>Same crowded bus as yesterday. Nothing has improved.</td></tr><tr><td>307 Temporary Redirect</td><td>Detour. You'll get where you're going. Eventually.</td></tr><tr><td>400 Bad Request</td><td>You tried to board with exact change. The machine only takes cards today.</td></tr><tr><td>403 Forbidden</td><td>Bus full. The driver won't even make eye contact.</td></tr><tr><td>404 Not Found</td><td>Stop not on this route. You're on the express. It's not your express.</td></tr><tr><td>408 Request Timeout</td><td>You waited twenty minutes. The app said "arriving now" twenty minutes ago.</td></tr><tr><td>410 Gone</td><td>That route was discontinued in 2019. The sign is still up. Nobody told it.</td></tr><tr><td>429 Too Many Requests</td><td>Everyone trying to board at once. Polite pushing ensues.</td></tr><tr><td>500 Internal Server Error</td><td>Signal failure. Nobody knows anything. We all stare at the tracks.</td></tr><tr><td>502 Bad Gateway</td><td>Transfer station closed. You cannot reach your connecting line.</td></tr><tr><td>503 Service Unavailable</td><td>Strike day. The bus is a rumor.</td></tr><tr><td>504 Gateway Timeout</td><td>Bus was supposed to arrive at 8:04. It is now 8:41.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>	<div class="card"><div class="card-title">HTTP Codes for Public Transit</div><p class="