34.17.1	http_status_table/HTTP Codes for Grocery Shopping	<div class="card"><div class="card-title">HTTP Codes for Grocery Shopping</div><p class="muted"><regex>user_name</regex>, the grocery store is a server with terrible inventory management.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Code</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>200 OK</td><td>Everything on your list. In stock. On sale. You are unstoppable.</td></tr><tr><td>206 Partial Content</td><td>Got the eggs and milk. The bread was a lie.</td></tr><tr><td>301 Moved Permanently</td><td>They rearranged the whole store again. Nothing is where it was.</td></tr><tr><td>304 Not Modified</td><td>Same sad produce section as last week. The lettuce hasn't forgiven you.</td></tr><tr><td>400 Bad Request</td><td>You brought a basket to a big-shop run. Rookie move.</td></tr><tr><td>401 Unauthorized</td><td>Loyalty card required for that price. You forgot yours. Again.</td></tr><tr><td>403 Forbidden</td><td>Self-checkout flagged you for "unexpected item in bagging area."</td></tr><tr><td>404 Not Found</td><td>The specific brand you came for no longer exists. Sorry.</td></tr><tr><td>408 Request Timeout</td><td>You spent forty minutes comparing pasta sauces. Your ice cream is melting.</td></tr><tr><td>409 Conflict</td><td>You and another shopper both reached for the last rotisserie chicken.</td></tr><tr><td>410 Gone</td><td>They discontinued your favorite yogurt. No warning. No mercy.</td></tr><tr><td>429 Too Many Requests</td><td>Sunday afternoon. Everyone is here. The aisles are a mosh pit.</td></tr><tr><td>500 Internal Server Error</td><td>Register crashed mid-scan. The cashier sighs deeply.</td></tr><tr><td>503 Service Unavailable</td><td>Store closed for restocking. Come back at 6am like a gremlin.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>	<div class="card"><div class="card-title">HTTP Codes for Grocery Shopping</div><p class="muted">, the grocery store is a server with terrible inventory management.</p><div 