34.18.1	http_status_table/HTTP Codes for Online Dating Messages	<div class="card"><div class="card-title">HTTP Codes for Online Dating Messages</div><p class="muted">The hardest API, <regex>user_name</regex>. Every message is a request. Not every request gets a response.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Code</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>100 Continue</td><td>They replied "haha." Not a full response, but the connection is still open.</td></tr><tr><td>200 OK</td><td>They matched your energy. Conversation flowing. Plans vaguely mentioned.</td></tr><tr><td>202 Accepted</td><td>They saw it, hearted it, and are composing something. Give it time.</td></tr><tr><td>204 No Content</td><td>Left on read. No reply. Just the little gray timestamp mocking you.</td></tr><tr><td>301 Moved Permanently</td><td>They moved the chat to another app. "This one's glitchy." Sure it is.</td></tr><tr><td>304 Not Modified</td><td>Same "hey how's your week going" as last time. No new information.</td></tr><tr><td>401 Unauthorized</td><td>You asked for their number too soon. Access denied.</td></tr><tr><td>403 Forbidden</td><td>You've been unmatched. No further communication is permitted.</td></tr><tr><td>404 Not Found</td><td>Their profile disappeared. They either deleted it or blocked you. Mystery.</td></tr><tr><td>408 Request Timeout</td><td>Three weeks since your last message. The conversation has quietly expired.</td></tr><tr><td>409 Conflict</td><td>You both tried to plan a date at the same time. Now it's awkward.</td></tr><tr><td>429 Too Many Requests</td><td>You double-texted. Then triple-texted. They're overwhelmed.</td></tr><tr><td>500 Internal Server Error</td><td>You sent a long paragraph about your ex. The app cannot process this.</td></tr><tr><td>503 Service Unavailable</td><td>They're "taking a break from dating apps." We've all said that.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>	<div class="card"><div class="card-title">HTTP Codes for Online Dating M