35.12.0	html_cheat_sheet/Kitchen Substitutions Cheat Sheet	<div class="umi-page"><div class="stack"><p class="muted">Hey <regex>user_name</regex>, pantry gaps happen. Here's the swap list I keep taped inside a cabinet door.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Missing</th><th>Use instead</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Buttermilk (1 cup)</td><td>1 tbsp lemon juice or vinegar + milk to 1 cup; rest 5 min</td></tr><tr><td>Baking powder (1 tsp)</td><td>1/4 tsp baking soda + 1/2 tsp cream of tartar</td></tr><tr><td>Egg (1)</td><td>1 tbsp ground flax + 3 tbsp water; rest 5 min</td></tr><tr><td>Heavy cream (1 cup)</td><td>3/4 cup milk + 1/4 cup melted butter</td></tr><tr><td>Brown sugar (1 cup)</td><td>1 cup white sugar + 1 tbsp molasses</td></tr><tr><td>Soy sauce</td><td>Tamari, or coconut aminos for less salt</td></tr><tr><td>Cornstarch (1 tbsp)</td><td>2 tbsp flour</td></tr><tr><td>Fresh herbs (1 tbsp)</td><td>1 tsp dried</td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class="acc"><summary>Sourdough starter swap?</summary><div class="body"><p class="t-small">Use 1/2 cup plain yogurt + 1/2 cup flour per cup of starter, plus 1 tsp baking soda. Rise is faster, tang is milder.</p></div></details><p class="dim t-small">Salt, fat, acid, heat: fix one and the dish usually forgives you.</p></div></div>	<div class="umi-page"><div class="stack"><p class="muted">Hey , pantry gaps happen. Here's the swap list I keep taped inside a cabinet door.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Missing</th><th>Use instead</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Buttermilk (1 cup)</td><td>1 tbsp lemon juice or vinegar + milk to 1 cup; rest 5 min</td></tr><tr><td>Baking powder (1 tsp)</td><td>1/4 tsp baking soda + 1/2 tsp cream of tartar</td></tr><tr><td>Egg (1)</td><td>1 tbsp ground flax + 3 tbsp water; rest 5 min</td></tr><tr><td>Heavy cream (1 cup)</td><td>3/4 cup milk + 1/4 cup melted butter</td></tr><tr><td>Brown sugar (1 cup)</td><td>1 cup white sugar + 1 tbsp molasses</td></tr><tr><td>Soy sauce</td><td>Tamari, or coconut aminos for less salt</td></tr><tr><td>Cornstarch (1 tbsp)</td><td>2 tbsp flour</td></tr><tr><td>Fresh herbs (1 tbsp)</td><td>1 tsp dried</td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class="acc"><summary>Sourdough starter swap?</summary><div class="body"><p class="t-small">Use 1/2 cup plain yogurt + 1/2 cup flour per cup of starter, plus 1 tsp baking soda. Rise is faster, tang is milder.</p></div></details><p class="dim t-small">Salt, fat, acid, heat: fix one and the dish usually forgives you.</p></div></div>	-
35.13.0	html_cheat_sheet/Sleep Hygiene Cheat Sheet	<div class="umi-page"><div class="stack"><p class="muted">Evening, <regex>user_name</regex>. Sleep is mostly a scheduling problem, not a willpower one.</p><div class="grid two"><div class="stat"><span class="label">Wind-down</span><span class="value">30–60<span class="unit"> min</span></span></div><div class="stat"><span class="label">Room temp</span><span class="value">65–68<span class="unit">°F</span></span></div><div class="stat"><span class="label">Caffeine cutoff</span><span class="value">2<span class="unit"> pm</span></span></div><div class="stat"><span class="label">Morning light</span><span class="value">10<span class="unit"> min</span></span></div></div><ul class="list"><li>Same wake time daily, weekends included.</li><li>Bed is for sleep; read elsewhere.</li><li>No screens 30 min before bed, or dim them hard.</li><li>If awake 20 min, get up and do something dull in low light.</li><li>Keep a 3am worry list by the bed; write, then close it.</li></ul><div class="callout info"><p class="t-small">Snoring plus daytime exhaustion? That's a doctor conversation, not a habit fix.</p></div><details class="acc"><summary>Naps: friend or foe?</summary><div class="body"><p class="t-small">20 minutes before 3pm is fine. Longer or later steals tonight's pressure to sleep.</p></div></details></div></div>	<div class="umi-page"><div class="stack"><p class="muted">Evening, . Sleep is mostly a scheduling problem, not a willpower one.</p><div class="grid two"><div class="stat"><span class="label">Wind-down</span><span class="value">30–60<span class="unit"> min</span></span></div><div class="stat"><span class="label">Room temp</span><span class="value">65–68<span class="unit">°F</span></span></div><div class="stat"><span class="label">Caffeine cutoff</span><span class="value">2<span class="unit"> pm</span></span></div><div class="stat"><span class="label">Morning light</span><span class="value">10<span class="unit"> min</span></span></div></div><ul class="list"><li>Same wake time daily, weekends included.</li><li>Bed is for sleep; read elsewhere.</li><li>No screens 30 min before bed, or dim them hard.</li><li>If awake 20 min, get up and do something dull in low light.</li><li>Keep a 3am worry list by the bed; write, then close it.</li></ul><div class="callout info"><p class="t-small">Snoring plus daytime exhaustion? That's a doctor conversation, not a habit fix.</p></div><details class="acc"><summary>Naps: friend or foe?</summary><div class="body"><p class="t-small">20 minutes before 3pm is fine. Longer or later steals tonight's pressure to sleep.</p></div></details></div></div>	-
35.14.0	html_cheat_sheet/Tipping Cheat Sheet	<div class="umi-page"><div class="stack"><p class="muted">Tipping runs on local custom, <regex>user_name>. Here's the common US range so you're never doing math at the table.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th class="num">Typical</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Restaurant, table service</td><td class="num">18–20%</td></tr><tr><td>Bar drinks</td><td class="num">$1–2/drink</td></tr><tr><td>Food delivery</td><td class="num">15–20%</td></tr><tr><td>Coffee counter</td><td class="num">$1 or spare change</td></tr><tr><td>Haircut or salon</td><td class="num">15–20%</td></tr><tr><td>Taxi or rideshare</td><td class="num">10–15%</td></tr><tr><td>Hotel housekeeping</td><td class="num">$2–5/night</td></tr><tr><td>Bellhop</td><td class="num">$1–2/bag</td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class="acc"><summary>Calculate 20% in your head</summary><div class="body"><p class="t-small">Move the decimal one spot left for 10%, double it. On $46: $4.60 and $9.20, so about $9.</p></div></details><div class="callout warn"><p class="t-small">Tip on the pre-tax total. On a card slip, write the tip clearly and keep your copy.</p></div></div></div>	<div class="umi-page"><div class="stack"><p class="muted">Tipping runs on local custom, <regex>user_name>. Here's the common US range so you're never doing math at the table.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th class="num">Typical</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Restaurant, table service</td><td class="num">18–20%</td></tr><tr><td>Bar drinks</td><td class="num">$1–2/drink</td></tr><tr><td>Food delivery</td><td class="num">15–20%</td></tr><tr><td>Coffee counter</td><td class="num">$1 or spare change</td></tr><tr><td>Haircut or salon</td><td class="num">15–20%</td></tr><tr><td>Taxi or rideshare</td><td class="num">10–15%</td></tr><tr><td>Hotel housekeeping</td><td class="num">$2–5/night</td></tr><tr><td>Bellhop</td><td class="num">$1–2/bag</td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class="acc"><summary>Calculate 20% in your head</summary><div class="body"><p class="t-small">Move the decimal one spot left for 10%, double it. On $46: $4.60 and $9.20, so about $9.</p></div></details><div class="callout warn"><p class="t-small">Tip on the pre-tax total. On a card slip, write the tip clearly and keep your copy.</p></div></div></div>	-
35.15.0	html_cheat_sheet/Paint a Room Cheat Sheet	<div class="umi-page"><div class="stack"><p class="muted">Half of painting is the boring hour before the brush, <regex>user_name</regex>.</p><ol class="list"><li>Clear the room or shove everything to the center; drop cloths everywhere.</li><li>Wash walls, fill nail holes, sand, and wipe the dust.</li><li>Blue tape the trim, outlets, and window edges.</li><li>Cut in a 2–3 in band along ceiling and corners first.</li><li>Roll in a W pattern, then fill it flat, keeping a wet edge.</li><li>Two thin coats beat one thick one. Wait the label's recoat time.</li><li>Pull tape while the final coat is just dry, not bone-dry.</li></ol><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Room</th><th>Sheen</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Bedroom, living</td><td>Matte or eggshell</td></tr><tr><td>Kitchen, bath</td><td>Satin</td></tr><tr><td>Trim, doors</td><td>Semi-gloss</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="callout good"><p class="t-small">One gallon covers about 350–400 sq ft per coat. Measure floor area and round up.</p></div></div></div>	<div class="umi-page"><div class="stack"><p class="muted">Half of painting is the boring hour before the brush, .</p><ol class="list"><li>Clear the room or shove everything to the center; drop cloths everywhere.</li><li>Wash walls, fill nail holes, sand, and wipe the dust.</li><li>Blue tape the trim, outlets, and window edges.</li><li>Cut in a 2–3 in band along ceiling and corners first.</li><li>Roll in a W pattern, then fill it flat, keeping a wet edge.</li><li>Two thin coats beat one thick one. Wait the label's recoat time.</li><li>Pull tape while the final coat is just dry, not bone-dry.</li></ol><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Room</th><th>Sheen</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Bedroom, living</td><td>Matte or eggshell</td></tr><tr><td>Kitchen, bath</td><td>Satin</td></tr><tr><td>Trim, doors</td><td>Semi-gloss</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="callout good"><p class="t-small">One gallon covers about 350–400 sq ft per coat. Measure floor area and round up.</p></div></div></div>	-
35.16.0	html_cheat_sheet/Phone Battery Cheat Sheet	<div class="umi-page"><div class="stack"><p class="muted">Batteries aren't mysterious, <regex>user_name</regex>. They just prefer the middle of the road.</p><div class="grid two"><div class="stat"><span class="label">Comfy range</span><span class="value">20–80<span class="unit">%</span></span></div><div class="stat"><span class="label">Hot is worse</span><span class="value">35<span class="unit">°C+</span></span></div></div><ul class="list"><li>Charge in small top-ups rather than 0 to 100 marathons.</li><li>Overnight is fine on modern phones; they taper the current.</li><li>Skip thick cases while fast charging, and never leave a phone on a hot dashboard.</li><li>Screen brightness and background location chew more than anything else.</li><li>Battery health drops naturally; under 80% is when replacements start paying off.</li></ul><details class="acc"><summary>Does closing background apps help?</summary><div class="body"><p class="t-small">Usually not. Reopening them costs more energy than leaving them parked.</p></div></details><div class="callout info"><p class="t-small">Use the maker's charger. Cheap bricks cut corners on heat and voltage.</p></div></div></div>	<div class="umi-page"><div class="stack"><p class="muted">Batteries aren't mysterious, . They just prefer the middle of the road.</p><div class="grid two"><div class="stat"><span class="label">Comfy range</span><span class="value">20–80<span class="unit">%</span></span></div><div class="stat"><span class="label">Hot is worse</span><span class="value">35<span class="unit">°C+</span></span></div></div><ul class="list"><li>Charge in small top-ups rather than 0 to 100 marathons.</li><li>Overnight is fine on modern phones; they taper the current.</li><li>Skip thick cases while fast charging, and never leave a phone on a hot dashboard.</li><li>Screen brightness and background location chew more than anything else.</li><li>Battery health drops naturally; under 80% is when replacements start paying off.</li></ul><details class="acc"><summary>Does closing background apps help?</summary><div class="body"><p class="t-small">Usually not. Reopening them costs more energy than leaving them parked.</p></div></details><div class="callout info"><p class="t-small">Use the maker's charger. Cheap bricks cut corners on heat and voltage.</p></div></div></div>	-
35.17.0	html_cheat_sheet/Bodyweight Workout Cheat Sheet	<div class="umi-page"><div class="stack"><p class="muted">No gym, no problem, <regex>user_name</regex>. Three rounds of this and you've done something real.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Move</th><th class="num">Reps</th><th>Works</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Squat</td><td class="num">12–15</td><td>Legs, glutes</td></tr><tr><td>Push-up</td><td class="num">8–12</td><td>Chest, arms</td></tr><tr><td>Reverse lunge</td><td class="num">10/leg</td><td>Legs, balance</td></tr><tr><td>Glute bridge</td><td class="num">15</td><td>Hips, lower back</td></tr><tr><td>Plank</td><td class="num">30–45 sec</td><td>Core</td></tr><tr><td>Bird dog</td><td class="num">8/side</td><td>Core, spine</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul class="list"><li>Warm up 3 min: march, arm circles, hip swings.</li><li>Rest 60 sec between rounds. Breathe through the hard parts.</li><li>Knees or incline push-ups are not cheating; they're the on-ramp.</li><li>Two or three sessions a week is plenty to start.</li></ul><details class="acc"><summary>How do I progress?</summary><div class="body"><p class="t-small">Add one rep a week, or slow the lowering phase to three seconds. Harder beats longer.</p></div></details></div></div>	<div class="umi-page"><div class="stack"><p class="muted">No gym, no problem, . Three rounds of this and you've done something real.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Move</th><th class="num">Reps</th><th>Works</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Squat</td><td class="num">12–15</td><td>Legs, glutes</td></tr><tr><td>Push-up</td><td class="num">8–12</td><td>Chest, arms</td></tr><tr><td>Reverse lunge</td><td class="num">10/leg</td><td>Legs, balance</td></tr><tr><td>Glute bridge</td><td class="num">15</td><td>Hips, lower back</td></tr><tr><td>Plank</td><td class="num">30–45 sec</td><td>Core</td></tr><tr><td>Bird dog</td><td class="num">8/side</td><td>Core, spine</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul class="list"><li>Warm up 3 min: march, arm circles, hip swings.</li><li>Rest 60 sec between rounds. Breathe through the hard parts.</li><li>Knees or incline push-ups are not cheating; they're the on-ramp.</li><li>Two or three sessions a week is plenty to start.</li></ul><details class="acc"><summary>How do I progress?</summary><div class="body"><p class="t-small">Add one rep a week, or slow the lowering phase to three seconds. Harder beats longer.</p></div></details></div></div>	-
35.18.0	html_cheat_sheet/Everyday Bike Maintenance Cheat Sheet	<div class="umi-page stack">  <div class="card">    <h2 class="card-title">Everyday Bike Maintenance <span class="badge accent"><i class="dot"></i>cached match</span></h2>    <p class="muted">Here you go, <regex>user_name</regex>. Ten minutes a week keeps the squeaks away.</p>    <div class="table-wrap">      <table>        <thead><tr><th>Check</th><th>How</th><th class="num">How often</th></tr></thead>        <tbody>          <tr><td>Tyre pressure</td><td>Squeeze the tyre; firm, not rock hard</td><td class="num">Every ride</td></tr>          <tr><td>Brakes</td><td>Lever should bite before it hits the bar</td><td class="num">Weekly</td></tr>          <tr><td>Chain</td><td>Wipe, then one drop of lube per link</td><td class="num">Weekly</td></tr>          <tr><td>Bolts</td><td>Quick wiggle of stem, seat, rack</td><td class="num">Monthly</td></tr>          <tr><td>Tyres</td><td>Look for glass, cracks, bald spots</td><td class="num">Monthly</td></tr>          <tr><td>Cables</td><td>Frayed ends? Replace them</td><td class="num">Yearly</td></tr>        </tbody>      </table>    </div>  </div>  <details class="acc">    <summary>The 60-second pre-ride check</summary>    <div class="body stack">      <p class="t-small">ABC, in order: <strong>Air</strong> in the tyres, <strong>Brakes</strong> squeeze both levers, <strong>Chain</strong> spin the pedals backwards and listen.</p>      <p class="t-small muted">Add D for <em>Drop</em>: lift the bike a hand's width and drop it. Anything rattles, tighten it.</p>    </div>  </details>  <div class="callout warn">    <p class="t-small">A chain that squeaks is dry, not broken. A chain that skips is worn and needs replacing.</p>  </div></div>	<div class="umi-page stack">  <div class="card">    <h2 class="card-title">Everyday Bike Maintenance <span class="badge accent"><i class="dot"></i>cached match</span></h2>    <p class="muted">Here you go, . Ten minutes a week keeps the squeaks away.</p>    <div class="table-wrap">      <table>        <thead><tr><th>Check</th><th>How</th><th class="num">How often</th></tr></thead>        <tbody>          <tr><td>Tyre pressure</td><td>Squeeze the tyre; firm, not rock hard</td><td class="num">Every ride</td></tr>          <tr><td>Brakes</td><td>Lever should bite before it hits the bar</td><td class="num">Weekly</td></tr>          <tr><td>Chain</td><td>Wipe, then one drop of lube per link</td><td class="num">Weekly</td></tr>          <tr><td>Bolts</td><td>Quick wiggle of stem, seat, rack</td><td class="num">Monthly</td></tr>          <tr><td>Tyres</td><td>Look for glass, cracks, bald spots</td><td class="num">Monthly</td></tr>          <tr><td>Cables</td><td>Frayed ends? Replace them</td><td class="num">Yearly</td></tr>        </tbody>      </table>    </div>  </div>  <details class="acc">    <summary>The 60-second pre-ride check</summary>    <div class="body stack">      <p class="t-small">ABC, in order: <strong>Air</strong> in the tyres, <strong>Brakes</strong> squeeze both levers, <strong>Chain</strong> spin the pedals backwards and listen.</p>      <p class="t-small muted">Add D for <em>Drop</em>: lift the bike a hand's width and drop it. Anything rattles, tighten it.</p>    </div>  </details>  <div class="callout warn">    <p class="t-small">A chain that squeaks is dry, not broken. A chain that skips is worn and needs replacing.</p>  </div></div>	-
35.19.0	html_cheat_sheet/Home Wi-Fi Troubleshooting Cheat Sheet	<div class="umi-page stack">  <div class="card">    <h2 class="card-title">Home Wi-Fi Troubleshooting <span class="badge accent"><i class="dot"></i>cached match</span></h2>    <p class="muted">Wi-Fi is mostly physics, <regex>user_name</regex>. Walls and microwaves don't negotiate.</p>    <div class="table-wrap">      <table>        <thead><tr><th>Symptom</th><th>Likely cause</th><th>Fix</th></tr></thead>        <tbody>          <tr><td>Drops at one spot</td><td>Distance or wall</td><td>Move router central, higher</td></tr>          <tr><td>Slow all day</td><td>Too many devices</td><td>Pause big downloads</td></tr>          <tr><td>Slow 7-9pm</td><td>Neighbour congestion</td><td>Switch to 5 GHz band</td></tr>          <tr><td>Dies at 2.4 GHz only</td><td>Microwave, baby monitor</td><td>Move router away</td></tr>          <tr><td>Fine wired, bad wireless</td><td>Router, not provider</td><td>Reboot router first</td></tr>        </tbody>      </table>    </div>  </div>  <details class="acc">    <summary>The reboot that actually works</summary>    <div class="body stack">      <ol class="list">        <li>Unplug the router for a full 30 seconds.</li>        <li>Plug in, wait two minutes for lights to settle.</li>        <li>Test one device close to the router, then one far away.</li>      </ol>      <p class="t-small muted">Bands, in plain terms: 2.4 GHz travels far and slow, 5 GHz is fast but shy.</p>    </div>  </details></div>	<div class="umi-page stack">  <div class="card">    <h2 class="card-title">Home Wi-Fi Troubleshooting <span class="badge accent"><i class="dot"></i>cached match</span></h2>    <p class="muted">Wi-Fi is mostly physics, . Walls and microwaves don't negotiate.</p>    <div class="table-wrap">      <table>        <thead><tr><th>Symptom</th><th>Likely cause</th><th>Fix</th></tr></thead>        <tbody>          <tr><td>Drops at one spot</td><td>Distance or wall</td><td>Move router central, higher</td></tr>          <tr><td>Slow all day</td><td>Too many devices</td><td>Pause big downloads</td></tr>          <tr><td>Slow 7-9pm</td><td>Neighbour congestion</td><td>Switch to 5 GHz band</td></tr>          <tr><td>Dies at 2.4 GHz only</td><td>Microwave, baby monitor</td><td>Move router away</td></tr>          <tr><td>Fine wired, bad wireless</td><td>Router, not provider</td><td>Reboot router first</td></tr>        </tbody>      </table>    </div>  </div>  <details class="acc">    <summary>The reboot that actually works</summary>    <div class="body stack">      <ol class="list">        <li>Unplug the router for a full 30 seconds.</li>        <li>Plug in, wait two minutes for lights to settle.</li>        <li>Test one device close to the router, then one far away.</li>      </ol>      <p class="t-small muted">Bands, in plain terms: 2.4 GHz travels far and slow, 5 GHz is fast but shy.</p>    </div>  </details></div>	-
