35.24.0	html_cheat_sheet/Kitchen Knife Skills Cheat Sheet	<div class="umi-page">  <div class="card">    <div class="card-title">Knife Cuts, Decoded</div>    <p class="muted">Hey <regex>user_name</regex> — most of the work is in the grip, not the blade. Pinch the blade, curl your guiding fingers, and let the knife do the falling.</p>    <div class="table-wrap">      <table>        <thead><tr><th>Cut</th><th>Size</th><th>Use</th></tr></thead>        <tbody>          <tr><td>Chop</td><td>Rough, ~2 cm</td><td>Soups, stews</td></tr>          <tr><td>Dice</td><td>Even cubes</td><td>Sauces, roasting</td></tr>          <tr><td>Mince</td><td>Finest bits</td><td>Garlic, ginger</td></tr>          <tr><td>Julienne</td><td>Matchsticks</td><td>Stir-fry</td></tr>          <tr><td>Chiffonade</td><td>Thin ribbons</td><td>Herbs, greens</td></tr>        </tbody>      </table>    </div>    <details class="acc">      <summary>Grip &amp; safety, quick version</summary>      <div class="body">        <ul class="list">          <li><strong>Pinch grip:</strong> thumb and index on the blade, remaining fingers wrap the handle.</li>          <li><strong>Claw:</strong> guiding hand curls, knuckles guide the blade.</li>          <li><strong>Sharp beats fast.</strong> A dull knife slips; a sharp one bites where you aim.</li>        </ul>      </div>    </details>    <div class="callout info">Onion tears? Chill it 15 minutes first. Cold slows the irritant, not your hands.</div>  </div></div>	<div class="umi-page">  <div class="card">    <div class="card-title">Knife Cuts, Decoded</div>    <p class="muted">Hey  — most of the work is in the grip, not the blade. Pinch the blade, curl your guiding fingers, and let the knife do the falling.</p>    <div class="table-wrap">      <table>        <thead><tr><th>Cut</th><th>Size</th><th>Use</th></tr></thead>        <tbody>          <tr><td>Chop</td><td>Rough, ~2 cm</td><td>Soups, stews</td></tr>          <tr><td>Dice</td>