35.27.0	html_cheat_sheet/Time Management Cheat Sheet	<div class="umi-page">  <div class="card">    <div class="card-title">Time, Sorted Without the Shame</div>    <p class="muted">Hi <regex>user_name</regex> — productivity isn't doing more. It's deciding what gets your best hours.</p>    <details class="acc" open>      <summary>Pomodoro, in practice</summary>      <div class="body">        <ol class="list">          <li>Pick one task. Only one.</li>          <li>Set a timer for 25 minutes.</li>          <li>Work until it rings.</li>          <li>Take 5 minutes off.</li>          <li>Every 4 rounds, rest 15–30 minutes.</li>        </ol>      </div>    </details>    <div class="table-wrap">      <table>        <thead><tr><th></th><th>Urgent</th><th>Not urgent</th></tr></thead>        <tbody>          <tr><td><strong>Important</strong></td><td>Do now</td><td>Schedule it</td></tr>          <tr><td><strong>Not important</strong></td><td>Delegate or shrink</td><td>Delete it</td></tr>        </tbody>      </table>    </div>    <div class="callout warn">If a task has been on your list for three weeks, it needs a 15-minute version, not more willpower.</div>  </div></div>	<div class="umi-page">  <div class="card">    <div class="card-title">Time, Sorted Without the Shame</div>    <p class="muted">Hi  — productivity isn't doing more. It's deciding what gets your best hours.</p>    <details class="acc" open>      <summary>Pomodoro, in practice</summary>      <div class="body">        <ol class="list">          <li>Pick one task. Only one.</li>          <li>Set a timer for 25 minutes.</li>          <li>Work until it rings.</li>          <li>Take 5 minutes off.</li>          <li>Every 4 rounds, rest 15–30 minutes.</li>        </ol>      </div>    </details>    <div class="table-wrap">      <table>        <thead><tr><th></th><th>Urgent</th><th>Not urgent</th></tr></thead>        <tbody>          <tr><td><strong>Important</strong></td><td>Do now</td><td>Schedule it</td></tr>          <tr><td><strong>Not important</strong></td><td>Delegate or shrink</td><td>Delete it</td></tr>        </tbody>      </table>    </div>    <div class="callout warn">If a task has been on your list for three weeks, it needs a 15-minute version, not more willpower.</div>  </div></div>	-
35.28.0	html_cheat_sheet/Sewing &amp; Mending Cheat Sheet	<div class="umi-page">  <div class="card">    <div class="card-title">Mend It, Wear It Longer</div>    <p class="muted">Hey <regex>user_name</regex> — a needle, thread, and ten minutes can rescue half your wardrobe. Start with these five stitches.</p>    <div class="table-wrap">      <table>        <thead><tr><th>Stitch</th><th>Best for</th></tr></thead>        <tbody>          <tr><td>Running</td><td>Quick seams, gathering</td></tr>          <tr><td>Backstitch</td><td>Strong seams that hold</td></tr>          <tr><td>Whip</td><td>Edges, closing gaps</td></tr>          <tr><td>Blanket</td><td>Felt, fleece, raw edges</td></tr>          <tr><td>Ladder</td><td>Invisible hems on knits</td></tr>        </tbody>      </table>    </div>    <details class="acc">      <summary>Sew a button back on</summary>      <div class="body">        <ol class="list">          <li>Mark the spot with a pin.</li>          <li>Thread the needle, knot the end.</li>          <li>Come up through one hole, down through another.</li>          <li>Repeat 4–6 times, then wrap the thread under the button a few turns for a shank.</li>          <li>Knot on the back and snip.</li>        </ol>      </div>    </details>    <div class="callout info">Match thread to fabric, not the button. It hides better.</div>  </div></div>	<div class="umi-page">  <div class="card">    <div class="card-title">Mend It, Wear It Longer</div>    <p class="muted">Hey  — a needle, thread, and ten minutes can rescue half your wardrobe. Start with these five stitches.</p>    <div class="table-wrap">      <table>        <thead><tr><th>Stitch</th><th>Best for</th></tr></thead>        <tbody>          <tr><td>Running</td><td>Quick seams, gathering</td></tr>          <tr><td>Backstitch</td><td>Strong seams that hold</td></tr>          <tr><td>Whip</td><td>Edges, closing gaps</td></tr>          <tr><td>Blanket</td><td>Felt, fleece, raw edges</td></tr>          <tr><td>Ladder</td><td>Invisible hems on knits</td></tr>        </tbody>      </table>    </div>    <details class="acc">      <summary>Sew a button back on</summary>      <div class="body">        <ol class="list">          <li>Mark the spot with a pin.</li>          <li>Thread the needle, knot the end.</li>          <li>Come up through one hole, down through another.</li>          <li>Repeat 4–6 times, then wrap the thread under the button a few turns for a shank.</li>          <li>Knot on the back and snip.</li>        </ol>      </div>    </details>    <div class="callout info">Match thread to fabric, not the button. It hides better.</div>  </div></div>	-
35.29.0	html_cheat_sheet/First Apartment Setup Cheat Sheet	<div class="umi-page">  <div class="card">    <div class="card-title">First Apartment, Fewer Panic Buys</div>    <p class="muted">Welcome, <regex>user_name</regex>. You need less than the internet says. These are the actual essentials.</p>    <div class="grid two">      <div class="stat"><div class="label">Deposit</div><div class="value">1–2 <span class="unit">months rent</span></div></div>      <div class="stat"><div class="label">Setup buffer</div><div class="value">$200–500</div></div>    </div>    <details class="acc" open>      <summary>The short list</summary>      <div class="body">        <ul class="list">          <li><strong>Bedroom:</strong> bed, sheets, pillow, lamp, blackout curtain.</li>          <li><strong>Kitchen:</strong> pot, pan, spatula, knife, cutting board, can opener, plates, cups.</li>          <li><strong>Bathroom:</strong> shower curtain, towels, plunger, toilet brush, toilet paper.</li>          <li><strong>Cleaning:</strong> all-purpose spray, broom or vacuum, trash bags, dish soap.</li>        </ul>      </div>    </details>    <details class="acc">      <summary>Utilities and admin</summary>      <div class="body">        <ol class="list">          <li>Photograph the unit before moving anything in.</li>          <li>Transfer or start electric, gas, water, internet.</li>          <li>Update your address: bank, ID, subscriptions.</li>          <li>Get renter's insurance — it's usually cheap per month.</li>        </ol>      </div>    </details>    <div class="callout good">Buy the boring things first. Decor can wait until you know how the light hits.</div>  </div></div>	<div class="umi-page">  <div class="card">    <div class="card-title">First Apartment, Fewer Panic Buys</div>    <p class="muted">Welcome, . You need less than the internet says. These are the actual essentials.</p>    <div class="grid two">      <div class="stat"><div class="l