35.50.0	html_cheat_sheet/Everyday Bike Commuting Cheat Sheet	<section class="umi-page stack">  <h2>Everyday Bike Commuting Cheat Sheet</h2>  <p class="muted">Two wheels, fewer parking tickets. Let's get you rolling, <regex>user_name</regex>.</p>  <div class="callout good"><strong>Golden rule:</strong> be predictable, be visible, be boring. Boring riders come home.</div>  <details class="acc" open>    <summary>Carry kit (the short list)</summary>    <div class="body">      <ul class="list">        <li>Spare tube + tire levers + mini pump or CO₂.</li>        <li>Multi-tool with the hex sizes your bike actually uses.</li>        <li>Lights: white front, red rear. Charge them weekly.</li>        <li>Lock that costs more than you'd like (see below).</li>        <li>Rain shell + a plastic bag for your phone/seat.</li>      </ul>    </div>  </details>  <details class="acc">    <summary>City survival moves</summary>    <div class="body">      <ol class="list">        <li>Ride a door's-width away from parked cars. Watch for brake lights and silhouettes.</li>        <li>Take the lane when it's too narrow to share. You're allowed.</li>        <li>Assume every driveway will produce a car. Greet the surprise before it greets you.</li>        <li>Signal with your arm. Eye contact beats a bell.</li>        <li>Pass on the left, announce it, don't buzz.</li>      </ol>      <div class="callout warn"><strong>Watch:</strong> right-turning trucks, bus blind spots, and anyone with a phone in hand.</div>    </div>  </details>  <details class="acc">    <summary>Locking up so it's still there</summary>    <div class="body">      <ul class="list">        <li>U-lock through frame + rear wheel, or frame + rack.</li>        <li>Lock to something bolted down that a thief can't lift the bike off of.</li>        <li>Remove quick-release front wheel or cable it.</li>        <li>Take lights, bag, and anything with a USB port.</li>        <li>Same spot every night? Vary it. Patterns get noticed.</li>      </ul>    </div>  </details>  <details class="acc">    <summary>Night &amp; rain</summary>    <div class="body">      <div class="table-wrap">        <table>          <thead><tr><th>Condition</th><th>Do this</th></tr></thead>          <tbody>            <tr><td>Dusk/night</td><td>Lights on, reflective ankle band</td></tr>            <tr><td>Rain</td><td>Lower tire pressure slightly, brake early</td></tr>            <tr><td>Wet paint/metal</td><td>Cross straight, don't turn on it</td></tr>            <tr><td>Fog</td><td>Blinky rear light, bright layer</td></tr>          </tbody>        </table>      </div>      <p class="t-small dim">Fenders are unglamorous and will change your life.</p>    </div>  </details>  <span class="badge accent"><i class="dot"></i>cached match</span></section>	<section class="umi-page stack">  <h2>Everyday Bike Commuting Cheat Sheet</h2>  <p class="muted">Two wheels, fewer parking tickets. Let's get you rolling, .</p>  <div class="callout good"><strong>Golden rule:</strong> be predictable, be visible, be boring. Boring riders come home.</div>  <details class="acc" open>    <summary>Carry kit (the short list)</summary>    <div class="body">      <ul class="list">        <li>Spare tube + tire levers + mini pump or CO₂.</li>        <li>Multi-tool with the hex sizes your bike actually uses.</li>        <li>Lights: white front, red rear. Charge them weekly.</li>        <li>Lock that costs more than you'd like (see below).</li>        <li>Rain shell + a plastic bag for your phone/seat.</li>      </ul>    </div>  </details>  <details class="acc">    <summary>City survival moves</summary>    <div class="body">      <ol class="list">        <li>Ride a door's-width away from parked cars. Watch for brake lights and silhouettes.</li>        <li>Take the lane when it's too narrow to share. You're allowed.</li>        <li>Assume every driveway will produce a ca