35.5.1	html_cheat_sheet/Everyday Wine Pairing Cheat Sheet	<div class="umi-page"><h2 class="card-title">Everyday Wine Pairing</h2><p class="muted">Rules are more like friendly suggestions. <regex>user_name</regex>, here are the ones that usually pay off.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Dish</th><th>Pour</th><th>Why</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Steak / lamb</td><td>Cabernet, Malbec</td><td>Tannin cuts through fat.</td></tr><tr><td>Roast chicken</td><td>Chardonnay, Pinot Noir</td><td>Flexible middleweights.</td></tr><tr><td>Fish / shellfish</td><td>Sauvignon Blanc, Albari&ntilde;o</td><td>Bright acid, no tannin clash.</td></tr><tr><td>Tomato pasta</td><td>Sangiovese, Barbera</td><td>Acid loves acid.</td></tr><tr><td>Spicy Thai / Indian</td><td>Off-dry Riesling</td><td>A touch of sugar tames heat.</td></tr><tr><td>Cheese board</td><td>Sparkling, Port</td><td>Bubbles cleanse; Port matches blue.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="callout info"><p><strong>When in doubt:</strong> match weight to weight. Delicate food, delicate wine.</p></div><details class="acc"><summary>If you only have one bottle</summary><div class="body"><p>Pinot Noir or dry Ros&eacute; plays nice with almost everything.</p></div></details></div>	<div class="umi-page"><h2 class="card-title">Everyday Wine Pairing</h2><p class="muted">Rules are more like friendly suggestions. , here are the ones that usually pay off.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Dish</th><th>Pour</th><th>Why</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Steak / lamb</td><td>Cabernet, Malbec</td><td>Tannin cuts through fat.</td></tr><tr><td>Roast chicken</td><td>Chardonnay, Pinot Noir</td><td>Flexible middleweights.</td></tr><tr><td>Fish / shellfish</td><td>Sauvignon Blanc, Albari&ntilde;o</td><td>Bright acid, no tannin clash.</td></tr><tr><td>Tomato pasta</td><td>Sangiovese, Barbera</td><td>Acid loves acid.</td></tr><tr><td>Spicy Thai / Indian</td><td>Off-dry Riesling</td><td>A touch of sugar tames heat.<