35.6.1	html_cheat_sheet/Everyday Home Recycling Cheat Sheet	<div class="umi-page"><h2 class="card-title">Everyday Home Recycling</h2><p class="muted">When in doubt, throw it out &mdash; wishcycling clogs the machines. <regex>user_name</regex>, quick rundown:</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Status</th><th>Note</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Plastic bottles &amp; jugs</td><td class="good">Recycle</td><td>#1 and #2 are gold. Rinse, cap on.</td></tr><tr><td>Glass jars &amp; bottles</td><td class="good">Recycle</td><td>Lids off unless your program says otherwise.</td></tr><tr><td>Aluminum cans &amp; foil</td><td class="good">Recycle</td><td>Ball up foil to fist size.</td></tr><tr><td>Cardboard</td><td class="good">Recycle</td><td>Flatten. Greasy pizza box? Tear off clean lid only.</td></tr><tr><td>Plastic bags &amp; wrap</td><td class="warn">Store drop-off</td><td>Never in curbside bins.</td></tr><tr><td>Styrofoam</td><td class="bad">Trash</td><td>Rarely accepted.</td></tr><tr><td>Batteries / e-waste</td><td class="bad">Special drop-off</td><td>Fire risk in trucks.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class="acc"><summary>Golden rules</summary><div class="body"><ul class="list"><li>Empty, rinse, dry.</li><li>No tanglers (hoses, cords, bagged stuff).</li><li>Check your city's app or site once &mdash; rules vary.</li></ul></div></details></div>	<div class="umi-page"><h2 class="card-title">Everyday Home Recycling</h2><p class="muted">When in doubt, throw it out &mdash; wishcycling clogs the machines. , quick rundown:</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Status</th><th>Note</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Plastic bottles &amp; jugs</td><td class="good">Recycle</td><td>#1 and #2 are gold. Rinse, cap on.</td></tr><tr><td>Glass jars &amp; bottles</td><td class="good">Recycle</td><td>Lids off unless your program says otherwise.</td></tr><tr><td>Aluminum cans &amp; foil</td><td class="good">Recycle</td><td>Ball up foil to