35.17.1	html_cheat_sheet/Everyday Board Game Etiquette Cheat Sheet	<div class="card">  <h3 class="card-title">Win Graciously, Lose Loudly (Kidding)</h3>  <p class="muted t-small">Turns out <regex>user_name</regex>, most game nights are won before anyone rolls a die.</p>  <div class="row"><span class="badge accent"><i class="dot"></i>Teach first</span><span class="badge info">Snack on the side table</span><span class="badge good">Rulebook stays open</span></div></div><details class="acc">  <summary>Teaching a new game (the 5-minute way)</summary>  <div class="body">    <ol class="list">      <li>Name the goal in one sentence.</li>      <li>What you do on a turn. Just that.</li>      <li>How the game ends and who wins.</li>      <li>Play one practice round with open hands.</li>      <li>Save edge cases until they come up.</li>    </ol>    <p class="dim t-small">Resist the full rules recital. Nobody remembers rule 4 of 12.</p>  </div></details><details class="acc">  <summary>House rules of decency</summary>  <div class="body">    <ul class="list">      <li>No phones at the table unless it's a rulebook look-up.</li>      <li>Announce your move, then move the piece.</li>      <li>Don't coach another player's turn unless asked — alpha gaming drains the table.</li>      <li>Take-backs: allow one, then hold the line, kindly.</li>      <li>Winner helps pack up. That's the real tax.</li>    </ul>  </div></details><details class="acc">  <summary>Handling the sore loser (or winner)</summary>  <div class="body">    <ul class="list">      <li>Pivot fast: "rematch or dessert?"</li>      <li>Praise a specific good play, not the result.</li>      <li>If it's a pattern, swap to co-op games for a while.</li>      <li>Don't relitigate the whole game in the post-mortem.</li>    </ul>  </div></details>	<div class="card">  <h3 class="card-title">Win Graciously, Lose Loudly (Kidding)</h3>  <p class="muted t-small">Turns out , most game nights are w