43.36.1	dashboard_tabs/Compost Pile Monitoring Dashboard	<div class="umi-page"><h1>Compost Pile Monitoring</h1><p class="muted">Hi <regex>user_name</regex> — three bins, one nose. Let's keep it aerobic.</p><div class="grid two"><div class="stat"><span class="label">Bin A temp</span><span class="value">142<span class="unit">°F</span></span><span class="delta">hot phase, day 4</span></div><div class="stat"><span class="label">Moisture</span><span class="value">54<span class="unit">%</span></span><span class="delta down">squeeze test: 2 drops</span></div><div class="stat"><span class="label">C:N ratio</span><span class="value">28<span class="unit">:1</span></span><span class="delta">target 25–30</span></div><div class="stat"><span class="label">Days since turn</span><span class="value">6</span><span class="delta down">turn by day 7</span></div></div><details class="tab"><summary>Temperature trend</summary><div class="body"><div class="chart"><svg viewBox="0 0 300 90"><polyline class="line" points="10,70 60,55 110,40 160,22 210,30 260,48"/><line class="axis" x1="10" y1="82" x2="290" y2="82"/><text class="lbl" x="10" y="14">150°F</text><text class="lbl" x="10" y="78">90°F</text></svg></div><ul class="list"><li>Peak 148°F on day 3 — pathogens gone.</li><li>Cooling slowly: normal after the hot phase.</li></ul></div></details><details class="tab"><summary>What went in</summary><div class="body"><ul class="list"><li>Greens: kitchen scraps, grass clippings, coffee grounds.</li><li>Browns: shredded cardboard, dry leaves, sawdust (untreated only).</li><li>Skip: meat, dairy, oils, pet waste, glossy paper.</li></ul><p class="t-small dim">If it stinks, add browns. If it's dry, add greens and a splash of water.</p></div></details><details class="tab"><summary>Turn log</summary><div class="body"><ul class="timeline"><li><span class="when">Day 6</span> Turned Bin A, moved outer layer to core.</li><li><span class="when">Day 3</span> First turn, added 2 cups shredded cardboard.</li><li><span class="when">Day 0</span> Rebuilt pile, 3:1 browns to greens.</li></ul></div></details></div>	<div class="umi-page"><h1>Compost Pile Monitoring</h1><p class="muted">Hi  — three bins, one nose. Let's keep it aerobic.</p><div class="grid two"><div class="stat"><span class="label">Bin A temp</span><span class="value">142<span class="unit">°F</span></span><span class="delta">hot phase, day 4</span></div><div class="stat"><span class="label">Moisture</span><span class="value">54<span class="unit">%</span></span><span class="delta down">squeeze test: 2 drops</span></div><div class="stat"><span class="label">C:N ratio</span><span class="value">28<span class="unit">:1</span></span><span class="delta">target 25–30</span></div><div class="stat"><span class="label">Days since turn</span><span class="value">6</span><span class="delta down">turn by day 7</span></div></div><details class="tab"><summary>Temperature trend</summary><div class="body"><div class="chart"><svg viewBox="0 0 300 90"><polyline class="line" points="10,70 60,55 110,40 160,22 210,30 260,48"/><line class="axis" x1="10" y1="82" x2="290" y2="82"/><text class="lbl" x="10" y="14">150°F</text><text class="lbl" x="10" y="78">90°F</text></svg></div><ul class="list"><li>Peak 148°F on day 3 — pathogens gone.</li><li>Cooling slowly: normal after the hot phase.</li></ul></div></details><details class="tab"><summary>What went in</summary><div class="body"><ul class="list"><li>Greens: kitchen scraps, grass clippings, coffee grounds.</li><li>Browns: shredded cardboard, dry leaves, sawdust (untreated only).</li><li>Skip: meat, dairy, oils, pet waste, glossy paper.</li></ul><p class="t-small dim">If it stinks, add browns. If it's dry, add greens and a splash of water.</p></div></details><details class="tab"><summary>Turn log</summary><div class="body"><ul class="timeline"><li><span class="when">Day 6</span> Turned Bin A, moved outer layer to core.</li><li><span class="when">Day 3</span> First turn, added 2 cups shredde