43.37.1	dashboard_tabs/Home Weightlifting Progress Dashboard	<div class="umi-page"><h1>Weightlifting Progress</h1><p class="muted">Hey <regex>user_name</regex> — slow is smooth, smooth is heavy.</p><div class="grid two"><div class="stat"><span class="label">Squat 1RM</span><span class="value">315<span class="unit">lb</span></span><span class="delta">+10 this block</span></div><div class="stat"><span class="label">Bench 1RM</span><span class="value">205<span class="unit">lb</span></span><span class="delta down">stalled 3 weeks</span></div><div class="stat"><span class="label">Deadlift 1RM</span><span class="value">405<span class="unit">lb</span></span><span class="delta">+15 this block</span></div><div class="stat"><span class="label">Weekly volume</span><span class="value">48,200<span class="unit">lb</span></span><span class="delta">sets×reps×load</span></div></div><details class="tab"><summary>This week's plan</summary><div class="body"><ul class="list"><li><strong>Mon</strong> Squat 5×5 @ 80% — 252 lb</li><li><strong>Wed</strong> Bench 5×5 @ 80% — 164 lb</li><li><strong>Fri</strong> Deadlift 3×3 @ 85% — 344 lb</li><li><strong>Sat</strong> Accessory: rows, dips, core</li></ul></div></details><details class="tab"><summary>Warm-up sets</summary><div class="body"><p class="t-small dim">Work up in steps — never jump straight to the top set.</p><ul class="list num"><li>Bar × 10</li><li>40% × 5</li><li>60% × 3</li><li>75% × 2</li><li>Work sets</li></ul></div></details><details class="tab"><summary>Fatigue cues</summary><div class="body"><div class="callout warn"><p>Bench tempo dropping two sessions in a row? Cut volume 20% and sleep more. Grinding reps builds fatigue, not strength.</p></div><ul class="list"><li>Bar speed off the chest</li><li>Grip slipping on deadlift lockout</li><li>Knees caving on heavy squat</li></ul></div></details><details class="tab"><summary>PR history</summary><div class="body"><ul class="timeline"><li><span class="when">Mar</span> Deadlift 405 —