43.40.1	dashboard_tabs/Home Piano Practice Dashboard	<div class="umi-page"><h1>Home Piano Practice</h1><p class="muted">Welcome back, <regex>user_name</regex>. Hands curved, shoulders down, coffee optional.</p><div class="grid two"><div class="stat"><span class="label">Streak</span><span class="value">14<span class="unit">days</span></span><span class="delta">longest yet</span></div><div class="stat"><span class="label">This week</span><span class="value">4.5<span class="unit">hrs</span></span><span class="delta">goal 5 hrs</span></div><div class="stat"><span class="label">Metronome</span><span class="value">72<span class="unit">BPM</span></span><span class="delta down">target 88</span></div><div class="stat"><span class="label">Current piece</span><span class="value">Gymnopédie No.1</span></div></div><details class="tab"><summary>Warm-up routine</summary><div class="body"><ul class="list"><li>C major scales, hands separately, 4 octaves</li><li>Hanon No. 1 at 72 BPM, then a notch up</li><li>Arpeggios: C, G, D, A</li><li>Two minutes of slow chord transitions</li></ul><p class="t-small dim">Five focused minutes beats thirty distracted ones.</p></div></details><details class="tab"><summary>Current repertoire</summary><div class="body"><ul class="list"><li><strong>Gymnopédie No. 1</strong> — dynamics, pedal half-down</li><li><strong>Prelude in C</strong> — memorize the last page</li><li><strong>Clair de Lune</strong> — section B, hands together slowly</li></ul></div></details><details class="tab"><summary>Practice log</summary><div class="body"><ul class="timeline"><li><span class="when">Today</span> 40 min — slow practice, no pedal.</li><li><span class="when">Yesterday</span> 30 min — hands separate, bars 16–24.</li><li><span class="when">Mon</span> 25 min — scales and sight reading.</li></ul></div></details><details class="tab"><summary>Stuck? Try this</summary><div class="body"><ul class="list"><li>Halve the tempo until it's boring, then rebuild.</li><li>Practice the two beats before and after the tricky bar.</li><li>Loop three bars, five clean times, then move on.</li></ul><div class="callout info"><p>Perfection ends up as repetition when you slow down — that's the trick, not a detour.</p></div></div></details></div>	<div class="umi-page"><h1>Home Piano Practice</h1><p class="muted">Welcome back, . Hands curved, shoulders down, coffee optional.</p><div class="grid two"><div class="stat"><span class="label">Streak</span><span class="value">14<span class="unit">days</span></span><span class="delta">longest yet</span></div><div class="stat"><span class="label">This week</span><span class="value">4.5<span class="unit">hrs</span></span><span class="delta">goal 5 hrs</span></div><div class="stat"><span class="label">Metronome</span><span class="value">72<span class="unit">BPM</span></span><span class="delta down">target 88</span></div><div class="stat"><span class="label">Current piece</span><span class="value">Gymnopédie No.1</span></div></div><details class="tab"><summary>Warm-up routine</summary><div class="body"><ul class="list"><li>C major scales, hands separately, 4 octaves</li><li>Hanon No. 1 at 72 BPM, then a notch up</li><li>Arpeggios: C, G, D, A</li><li>Two minutes of slow chord transitions</li></ul><p class="t-small dim">Five focused minutes beats thirty distracted ones.</p></div></details><details class="tab"><summary>Current repertoire</summary><div class="body"><ul class="list"><li><strong>Gymnopédie No. 1</strong> — dynamics, pedal half-down</li><li><strong>Prelude in C</strong> — memorize the last page</li><li><strong>Clair de Lune</strong> — section B, hands together slowly</li></ul></div></details><details class="tab"><summary>Practice log</summary><div class="body"><ul class="timeline"><li><span class="when">Today</span> 40 min — slow practice, no pedal.</li><li><span class="when">Yesterday</span> 30 min — hands separate, bars 16–24.</li><li><span class="when">Mon</span> 25 min — scales and sight reading.</li></ul