44.46.0	dashboard_timeline/Pottery Glazing Timeline	<div class="umi-page"><h1>Pottery Glazing Timeline</h1><div class="card"><h2 class="card-title">From Wheel to Shelf</h2><ul class="timeline"><li><span class="when">Day 0</span><p>Throw the piece. Cover loosely.</p></li><li><span class="when">Day 3</span><p>Trim the foot when leather-hard.</p></li><li><span class="when">Day 7</span><p>Bone dry. Ready for bisque.</p></li><li><span class="when">Day 8</span><p>Bisque fire to cone 06.</p></li><li><span class="when">Day 10</span><p>Wax resist the foot, then glaze.</p></li><li><span class="when">Day 11</span><p>Wipe glaze off the bottom. Important.</p></li><li><span class="when">Day 12</span><p>Glaze fire to cone 6.</p></li><li><span class="when">Day 13</span><p>Unload. Admire. Repeat.</p></li></ul></div><div class="callout warn"><p>Thick glaze pools and sticks to the kiln shelf. Two thin coats beat one glug, <regex>user_name</regex>.</p></div></div>	<div class="umi-page"><h1>Pottery Glazing Timeline</h1><div class="card"><h2 class="card-title">From Wheel to Shelf</h2><ul class="timeline"><li><span class="when">Day 0</span><p>Throw the piece. Cover loosely.</p></li><li><span class="when">Day 3</span><p>Trim the foot when leather-hard.</p></li><li><span class="when">Day 7</span><p>Bone dry. Ready for bisque.</p></li><li><span class="when">Day 8</span><p>Bisque fire to cone 06.</p></li><li><span class="when">Day 10</span><p>Wax resist the foot, then glaze.</p></li><li><span class="when">Day 11</span><p>Wipe glaze off the bottom. Important.</p></li><li><span class="when">Day 12</span><p>Glaze fire to cone 6.</p></li><li><span class="when">Day 13</span><p>Unload. Admire. Repeat.</p></li></ul></div><div class="callout warn"><p>Thick glaze pools and sticks to the kiln shelf. Two thin coats beat one glug, .</p></div></div>	-
44.47.0	dashboard_timeline/Bike Tune-Up Timeline	<div class="umi-page"><h1 class="card-title">Bike Tune-Up Timeline</h1><p class="muted">A calm hour in the stand. <regex>user_name</regex>, here's the order that keeps you from re-adjusting things twice.</p><ul class="timeline"><li><span class="when">0 min</span><p>Wipe the frame and drivetrain. A clean bike shows you the real problems.</p></li><li><span class="when">5 min</span><p>Check tire pressure and look for cuts or embedded glass. Inflate to sidewall spec.</p></li><li><span class="when">10 min</span><p>Inspect brake pads for wear and alignment. Replace if under 1 mm of pad left.</p></li><li><span class="when">20 min</span><p>Index the gears: shift through all cogs, adjust barrel adjuster a quarter turn at a time.</p></li><li><span class="when">35 min</span><p>Lube the chain, wipe excess. One drop per roller, backpedal, then rag.</p></li><li><span class="when">45 min</span><p>Torque check: stem, seatpost, pedals. A click at the right number saves a walk home.</p></li><li><span class="when">55 min</span><p>Test ride around the block. Listen for creaks and confirm smooth shifts.</p></li></ul><details class="acc"><summary>Quick check before you ride</summary><div class="body"><p>Spin the wheels. If they wobble, true them before the next long ride.</p></div></details></div>	<div class="umi-page"><h1 class="card-title">Bike Tune-Up Timeline</h1><p class="muted">A calm hour in the stand. , here's the order that keeps you from re-adjusting things twice.</p><ul class="timeline"><li><span class="when">0 min</span><p>Wipe the frame and drivetrain. A clean bike shows you the real problems.</p></li><li><span class="when">5 min</span><p>Check tire pressure and look for cuts or embedded glass. Inflate to sidewall spec.</p></li><li><span class="when">10 min</span><p>Inspect brake pads for wear and alignment. Replace if under 1 mm of pad left.</p></li><li><span class="when">20 min</span><p>Index the gears: shift through all cogs, adjust barrel adjuster a quarter turn at a time.</p></li><li><span class="when">35 min</span><p>Lube the chain, wipe excess. One drop per roller, backpedal, then rag.</p></li><li><span class="when">45 min</span><p>Torque check: stem, seatpost, pedals. A click at the right number saves a walk home.</p></li><li><span class="when">55 min</span><p>Test ride around the block. Listen for creaks and confirm smooth shifts.</p></li></ul><details class="acc"><summary>Quick check before you ride</summary><div class="body"><p>Spin the wheels. If they wobble, true them before the next long ride.</p></div></details></div>	-
44.48.0	dashboard_timeline/Cake Baking Timeline	<div class="umi-page"><h1 class="card-title">Cake Baking Timeline</h1><p class="muted">From cold butter to warm slice. <regex>user_name</regex>, give the oven a head start.</p><ul class="timeline"><li><span class="when">0 min</span><p>Pull butter and eggs out. Room temp is the quiet secret to a light crumb.</p></li><li><span class="when">10 min</span><p>Preheat to 350°F (175°C). Grease and line your pans.</p></li><li><span class="when">15 min</span><p>Cream butter and sugar until pale, about 4 minutes. Don't rush this.</p></li><li><span class="when">25 min</span><p>Add eggs one at a time, then alternate dry and wet ingredients.</p></li><li><span class="when">35 min</span><p>Divide batter evenly. Bake 25–30 min, rotating halfway.</p></li><li><span class="when">65 min</span><p>Cool in pans 10 min, then on a rack. Frost only when fully cool.</p></li></ul><div class="callout info"><p>Toothpick test: a few moist crumbs, not wet batter. That's your green light.</p></div></div>	<div class="umi-page"><h1 class="card-title">Cake Baking Timeline</h1><p class="muted">From cold butter to warm slice. , give the oven a head start.</p><ul class="timeline"><li><span class="when">0 min</span><p>Pull butter and eggs out. Room temp is the quiet secret to a light crumb.</p></li><li><span class="when">10 min</span><p>Preheat to 350°F (175°C). Grease and line your pans.</p></li><li><span class="when">15 min</span><p>Cream butter and sugar until pale, about 4 minutes. Don't rush this.</p></li><li><span class="when">25 min</span><p>Add eggs one at a time, then alternate dry and wet ingredients.</p></li><li><span class="when">35 min</span><p>Divide batter evenly. Bake 25–30 min, rotating halfway.</p></li><li><span class="when">65 min</span><p>Cool in pans 10 min, then on a rack. Frost only when fully cool.</p></li></ul><div class="callout info"><p>Toothpick test: a few moist crumbs, not wet batter. That's your green light.</p></div></div>	-
44.49.0	dashboard_timeline/Laundry Day Timeline	<div class="umi-page"><h1 class="card-title">Laundry Day Timeline</h1><p class="muted"><regex>user_name</regex>, a basket doesn't have to eat your whole afternoon. Here's the rhythm.</p><ul class="timeline"><li><span class="when">0 min</span><p>Sort into lights, darks, and delicates. Check pockets for rogue receipts.</p></li><li><span class="when">5 min</span><p>Start the first load. Cold water for colors, warm for whites.</p></li><li><span class="when">35 min</span><p>Move first load to dryer. Start second load while it runs.</p></li><li><span class="when">70 min</span><p>Fold first load while second washes. Multitasking without panic.</p></li><li><span class="when">100 min</span><p>Dry second load. Hang delicates to air dry.</p></li><li><span class="when">130 min</span><p>Fold everything, put away. The couch is not a dresser.</p></li></ul><details class="acc"><summary>Wrinkle rescue</summary><div class="body"><p>Throw a damp towel in the dryer for 10 min. Steam does the iron's job.</p></div></details></div>	<div class="umi-page"><h1 class="card-title">Laundry Day Timeline</h1><p class="muted">, a basket doesn't have to eat your whole afternoon. Here's the rhythm.</p><ul class="timeline"><li><span class="when">0 min</span><p>Sort into lights, darks, and delicates. Check pockets for rogue receipts.</p></li><li><span class="when">5 min</span><p>Start the first load. Cold water for colors, warm for whites.</p></li><li><span class="when">35 min</span><p>Move first load to dryer. Start second load while it runs.</p></li><li><span class="when">70 min</span><p>Fold first load while second washes. Multitasking without panic.</p></li><li><span class="when">100 min</span><p>Dry second load. Hang delicates to air dry.</p></li><li><span class="when">130 min</span><p>Fold everything, put away. The couch is not a dresser.</p></li></ul><details class="acc"><summary>Wrinkle rescue</summary><div class="body"><p>Throw a damp towel in the dryer for 10 min. Steam does the iron's job.</p></div></details></div>	-
44.50.0	dashboard_timeline/Moving Day Timeline	<div class="umi-page"><h1 class="card-title">Moving Day Timeline</h1><p class="muted">Boxes, keys, and a little chaos. <regex>user_name</regex>, a loose script helps more than a tight one.</p><ul class="timeline"><li><span class="when">6:00 AM</span><p>Wake up, coffee, pack the last-minute bag: toiletries, chargers, snacks.</p></li><li><span class="when">7:00 AM</span><p>Movers arrive (or friends). Label rooms clearly. Point, don't micromanage.</p></li><li><span class="when">9:00 AM</span><p>Truck loaded. Do a final walkthrough: closets, cabinets, outlets.</p></li><li><span class="when">10:00 AM</span><p>Drive to new place. Keep the essentials box with you, not in the truck.</p></li><li><span class="when">11:00 AM</span><p>Unload. Direct boxes to rooms. Set up beds first, then kitchen.</p></li><li><span class="when">2:00 PM</span><p>Return keys to old landlord if needed. Grab lunch. You earned it.</p></li><li><span class="when">4:00 PM</span><p>Unpack the kitchen and bathrooms. Everything else can wait a day.</p></li></ul><details class="acc"><summary>First night survival kit</summary><div class="body"><p>Toilet paper, hand soap, towels, one pot, one pan, and a bottle of wine.</p></div></details></div>	<div class="umi-page"><h1 class="card-title">Moving Day Timeline</h1><p class="muted">Boxes, keys, and a little chaos. , a loose script helps more than a tight one.</p><ul class="timeline"><li><span class="when">6:00 AM</span><p>Wake up, coffee, pack the last-minute bag: toiletries, chargers, snacks.</p></li><li><span class="when">7:00 AM</span><p>Movers arrive (or friends). Label rooms clearly. Point, don't micromanage.</p></li><li><span class="when">9:00 AM</span><p>Truck loaded. Do a final walkthrough: closets, cabinets, outlets.</p></li><li><span class="when">10:00 AM</span><p>Drive to new place. Keep the essentials box with you, not in the truck.</p></li><li><span class="when">11:00 AM</span><p>Unload. Direct boxes to rooms. Set up beds first, then kitchen.</p></li><li><span class="when">2:00 PM</span><p>Return keys to old landlord if needed. Grab lunch. You earned it.</p></li><li><span class="when">4:00 PM</span><p>Unpack the kitchen and bathrooms. Everything else can wait a day.</p></li></ul><details class="acc"><summary>First night survival kit</summary><div class="body"><p>Toilet paper, hand soap, towels, one pot, one pan, and a bottle of wine.</p></div></details></div>	-
44.51.0	dashboard_timeline/Grocery Run Timeline	<div class="umi-page"><h1>Grocery Run Timeline</h1><p class="muted">A tidy order of operations, <regex>user_name</regex>. Shop the perimeter last and nothing melts.</p><div class="card"><div class="card-title">Your route</div><ul class="timeline"><li><span class="when">Before</span><p>Check the fridge and pantry. Build the list by aisle, not by craving.</p></li><li><span class="when">0:00</span><p>Grab a cart with quiet wheels. Small wins matter.</p></li><li><span class="when">0:10</span><p>Produce first. Weigh, bag, and keep soft fruit on top of the pile.</p></li><li><span class="when">0:25</span><p>Dry goods and cans. This is where impulse buys sneak in; hold the line.</p></li><li><span class="when">0:40</span><p>Dairy and chilled items. Still cold, still fine.</p></li><li><span class="when">0:50</span><p>Meat and fish last. Ask for ice if the drive home is long.</p></li><li><span class="when">1:05</span><p>Checkout, then bag cold items together so they insulate each other.</p></li></ul></div><details class="acc"><summary>Note on timing</summary><div class="body"><p class="t-small">Weekday mornings before 11 are the calm window. Sunday after 4 is a contact sport.</p></div></details></div>	<div class="umi-page"><h1>Grocery Run Timeline</h1><p class="muted">A tidy order of operations, . Shop the perimeter last and nothing melts.</p><div class="card"><div class="card-title">Your route</div><ul class="timeline"><li><span class="when">Before</span><p>Check the fridge and pantry. Build the list by aisle, not by craving.</p></li><li><span class="when">0:00</span><p>Grab a cart with quiet wheels. Small wins matter.</p></li><li><span class="when">0:10</span><p>Produce first. Weigh, bag, and keep soft fruit on top of the pile.</p></li><li><span class="when">0:25</span><p>Dry goods and cans. This is where impulse buys sneak in; hold the line.</p></li><li><span class="when">0:40</span><p>Dairy and chilled items. Still cold, still fine.</p></li><li><span class="when">0:50</span><p>Meat and fish last. Ask for ice if the drive home is long.</p></li><li><span class="when">1:05</span><p>Checkout, then bag cold items together so they insulate each other.</p></li></ul></div><details class="acc"><summary>Note on timing</summary><div class="body"><p class="t-small">Weekday mornings before 11 are the calm window. Sunday after 4 is a contact sport.</p></div></details></div>	-
44.52.0	dashboard_timeline/Bread Proofing Timeline	<div class="umi-page"><h1>Bread Proofing Timeline</h1><p class="muted">Dough keeps its own clock, <regex>user_name</regex>. These are the checkpoints, not the law.</p><div class="grid two"><div class="stat"><span class="label">Bulk</span><span class="value">3<span class="unit">-5 h</span></span><span class="delta down">warm room</span></div><div class="stat"><span class="label">Final proof</span><span class="value">45<span class="unit">-90 min</span></span></div></div><div class="card"><div class="card-title">Checkpoints</div><ul class="timeline"><li><span class="when">0:00</span><p>Mix, rest 30 minutes, then fold. The dough looks shaggy. It is fine.</p></li><li><span class="when">0:30</span><p>First fold set. Four folds, 15 minutes apart.</p></li><li><span class="when">1:30</span><p>Bulk begins in earnest. Aim for a 50 percent rise, not a doubling.</p></li><li><span class="when">3:00</span><p>Poke test: the dent springs back slowly and stays a little.</p></li><li><span class="when">3:15</span><p>Shape and into the basket. Cold retard overnight if you like.</p></li><li><span class="when">Next day</span><p>Bake at 230C covered 20, uncovered 20. Cool one hour before slicing. Truly.</p></li></ul></div><div class="callout warn"><p class="t-small">If the dough is sticky and slack, it is underproofed, not ruined. Give it time.</p></div></div>	<div class="umi-page"><h1>Bread Proofing Timeline</h1><p class="muted">Dough keeps its own clock, . These are the checkpoints, not the law.</p><div class="grid two"><div class="stat"><span class="label">Bulk</span><span class="value">3<span class="unit">-5 h</span></span><span class="delta down">warm room</span></div><div class="stat"><span class="label">Final proof</span><span class="value">45<span class="unit">-90 min</span></span></div></div><div class="card"><div class="card-title">Checkpoints</div><ul class="timeline"><li><span class="when">0:00</span><p>Mix, rest 30 minutes, then fold. The dough looks shaggy. It is fine.</p></li><li><span class="when">0:30</span><p>First fold set. Four folds, 15 minutes apart.</p></li><li><span class="when">1:30</span><p>Bulk begins in earnest. Aim for a 50 percent rise, not a doubling.</p></li><li><span class="when">3:00</span><p>Poke test: the dent springs back slowly and stays a little.</p></li><li><span class="when">3:15</span><p>Shape and into the basket. Cold retard overnight if you like.</p></li><li><span class="when">Next day</span><p>Bake at 230C covered 20, uncovered 20. Cool one hour before slicing. Truly.</p></li></ul></div><div class="callout warn"><p class="t-small">If the dough is sticky and slack, it is underproofed, not ruined. Give it time.</p></div></div>	-
44.53.0	dashboard_timeline/Recovery Day Timeline	<div class="umi-page"><h1>Recovery Day Timeline</h1><p class="muted">Low effort, high returns, <regex>user_name</regex>. Cancel things. That is the plan.</p><div class="card"><ul class="timeline"><li><span class="when">Morning</span><p>Water by the bed before coffee. Take your temperature and note it.</p></li><li><span class="when">+1 h</span><p>Something warm and plain: toast, broth, rice. Small portions.</p></li><li><span class="when">Midday</span><p>Rest flat, not on the couch half-awake. Real horizontal rest.</p></li><li><span class="when">Afternoon</span><p>Electrolytes, a shower if you can stand it, then back down.</p></li><li><span class="when">Evening</span><p>Check in with your body. Fever climbing or breathing hard? Call someone.</p></li><li><span class="when">Night</span><p>Extra pillow, phone in another room, lights low.</p></li></ul></div><div class="callout info"><p class="t-small">This is comfort, not medicine. If you are worried, ask a clinician and trust that instinct.</p></div></div>	<div class="umi-page"><h1>Recovery Day Timeline</h1><p class="muted">Low effort, high returns, . Cancel things. That is the plan.</p><div class="card"><ul class="timeline"><li><span class="when">Morning</span><p>Water by the bed before coffee. Take your temperature and note it.</p></li><li><span class="when">+1 h</span><p>Something warm and plain: toast, broth, rice. Small portions.</p></li><li><span class="when">Midday</span><p>Rest flat, not on the couch half-awake. Real horizontal rest.</p></li><li><span class="when">Afternoon</span><p>Electrolytes, a shower if you can stand it, then back down.</p></li><li><span class="when">Evening</span><p>Check in with your body. Fever climbing or breathing hard? Call someone.</p></li><li><span class="when">Night</span><p>Extra pillow, phone in another room, lights low.</p></li></ul></div><div class="callout info"><p class="t-small">This is comfort, not medicine. If you are worried